{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat formal/checks_si.cfg && cat tools/eval/cosim.py && rg -n 'def |median|options|argparse|output|work_dir|build_dir|temp' tools/eval/gowin.py && git diff --stat\"", "aggregated_output": "[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n\"\"\"Runs Verilator cosim for all bench ELFs. Returns structured pass/fail.\n\nCorrectness is gated in two stages:\n  1. Full RVFI trace cosim for selftest and any other small ELF — every\n     retirement is diffed against the Python reference ISS.\n  2. CoreMark CRC validation via the sim's UART capture — full-trace cosim\n     of coremark.elf is skipped because the Python reference is ~10⁴× slower\n     than Verilator (would take 30+ minutes per candidate). Instead we run\n     the sim in --bench mode and verify its UART matches the canonical CRCs\n     with `validate_coremark_uart` (the same check run_fp\n…[8700 of 11772 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:44d7648a14bd0f02]…\nin_p{p}\", env) for p in options]\n179:def summarize(results: list[dict]) -> dict:\n180:    \"\"\"Median Fmax over placement options; every option must fit (the flow\n190:        \"fmax_mhz\": round(statistics.median(r[\"fmax_mhz\"] for r in results), 3),\n199:def main(argv=None) -> int:\n202:    import argparse, json\n204:    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n208:    ap.add_argument(\"--all-options\", action=\"store_true\",\n212:    opts = PLACE_OPTIONS if a.all_options else PLACE_OPTIONS[:1]\n214:                                wt / \"cores\" / a.target / \"generated\" / \"timing\", options=opts)\n227:        print(f\"score Fmax (median): {summarize(res)['fmax_mhz']} MHz\")\n cores/bench/rtl/core.sv        | 10 +++++++-\n cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv    |  2 ++\n cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv    | 31 +++++++++++++++---------\n cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv | 14 +++++++----\n cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv    |  5 ++++\n cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv    | 54 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------\n 6 files changed, 89 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
