Mark retirement against the unchanged interpreter and collecting the final timing results.\n\nplace_option 1: Fmax 55.621 MHz, 20 logic levels; logic 3659, registers 1072, LUT-RAM 8, BSRAM 6, DSP 2\nplace_option 2: Fmax 55.621 MHz, 20 logic levels; logic 3659, registers 1072, LUT-RAM 8, BSRAM 6, DSP 2\nplace_option 2: Fmax 55.621 MHz, 20 logic levels; logic 3659, registers 1072, LUT-RAM 8, BSRAM 6, DSP 2\nscore Fmax (median): 55.621 MHz\nThe full stalled CoreMark trace passed: all 2,937,037 retirements match the unchanged interpreter field by field. Final timing remains 55.621 MHz median, giving 131.21097 iterations/second. I stopped deep formal after 45 passes, the two signed-reference failures, and six unresolved arithmetic checks; those limits are recorded in the implementation notes.\n\n  \"cycles\": 4239051,\n  \"iterations\": 10,\nCycle increase: 35538\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
