{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_90", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r11s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261003-001-r11s0\ntitle: \"Speculate divider sign correction before final digit selection\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 133.79 at 56.239 MHz with 4,203,513 bracketed\n  CoreMark cycles. Its reported critical path runs from divider quotient\n  state to EX/MEM through two radix-4 digits and final sign correction.\n  The recent r10s0 micro_opt again ended on this path and lost 5.90%.\n  Earlier borrow-prefix restructuring lost to routing, while r9s1 moved\n  work into operand capture and exposed a competing multiplier path.\n  Target the serial correction after digit selection without changing\n  operand capture, divider scheduling, or any other execution unit.\nhypothesis: |\n  Compute negative divider results in parallel with the last radix-4\n  digit's candidate subtractions, rather than negating the already\n  selected full-width quotient or remainder. This is a local arithmetic\n  selection optimization: retain operand normalization, captured D and\n  3D, the two radix-4 digits per round, eight arithmetic rounds, and the\n  exact nine-clock request-to-EX/MEM transfer schedule.\n\n  Keep the positive recurrence and its full 35-bit borrow comparisons\n  unchanged. In the second digit, let T be the existing 34-bit trial\n  remainder and k be the selected digit in 0..3. Alongside its current\n  positive candidates T-kD, compute four negative-result candidates\n  (kD-T) modulo 2^32 for k=0,1,2,3. Use explicitly 32-bit arithmetic\n  on the low bits of T, D, 2D and 3D for these result candidates only.\n  The existing full-width comparisons still determine k; never truncate\n  their operands or derive selection from a modular candidate's sign.\n  Select the negative remainder with the existing mutually exclusive\n  digit masks. Since selected R=T-kD fits in 32 bits, this produces\n  exactly -R modulo 2^32, including D=0. The reverse subtractions run\n  in parallel with digit selection; do not describe them as negation\n  of selected_remainder, which recreates the original serial chain.\n\n  Remove the correspondin\n…[3154 of 6226 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3caaf890c2bd55c5]…\nas not yet been implemented or timed.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Add parallel reverse-subtraction candidates for the second radix-4\n      digit's final signed remainder and carry-select candidates for its\n      signed quotient. Select corrected candidates with the existing\n      full-width digit decisions and captured operation/sign controls.\n      Remove only the serial final selected-result negation. Preserve\n      unsigned recurrence, operand capture, exact completion timing,\n      held results, all other arithmetic and the ALTOPS branch.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Extend real divider tests to exercise every final radix-4 digit,\n      quotient carry boundaries, negative remainders, full-width trial\n      values, D=0 and signed overflow. Retain existing arithmetic,\n      recurrence, exact latency, backpressure, reset and transaction\n      assertions, and use an independent integer RV32M reference.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
