{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_2", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md; rg -n '\\\"category\\\":\\\\s*\\\"micro_opt\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r1s1 (improvement, +490.43%): Replacing combinational `/` and `%` in `alu.sv` with a registered divider limited to eight restoring steps per cycle shortened the clock-limiting arithmetic path enough to outweigh seven-clock DIV/REM latency in CoreMark.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r1s2 (regression, +7.01%): A 128-entry bimodal predictor plus direct-JAL prediction cut CoreMark cycles by 6.4% by removing redirect bubbles, but the unchanged forwarding/combinational-ALU critical path kept Fmax near 5.45 MHz, limiting the fitness gain over baseline to 7%.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r2s1 (improvement, +30.42%): Halving the divider's restoring recurrence from eight steps to four and fusing final-round sign correction into EX/MEM let reduced arithmetic depth outweigh the increase from seven to nine blocking DIV/REM clocks in CoreMark.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r2s2 (regression, +4.74%): Adding a 128-entry bimodal/JAL predictor cut CoreMark cycles by 6.4% but lowered median Fmax from 32.14 to 31.494 MHz with the unchanged divider still critical, showing that fetch-side additions can consume timing margin in unrelated arithmetic paths.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r3s0 (regression, -28.15%): Balanced four-bit borrow prefixes in `alu.sv` reduced critical-path cell count but left four restoring steps serial with routing dominating delay (~60%), lowering Gowin median Fmax from 41.919 to 30.118 MHz at unchanged CoreMark cycles; fewer arithmetic cells do not guarantee faster FPGA timing.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r3s1 (improvement, +11.34%): Parallel D/2D/3D trial subtraction with registered 3D and one-hot selection in `alu.sv` shortened each divider round from four dependent radix-2 steps to two radix-4 digits, improving fitness without increasing the nine-clock DIV/REM latency.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r4s0 (regression, +8.24%): Removing the IF instruction-to-NOP mux shortened the redirect-to-hazard control path and raised median Gowin Fmax to 50.514 MHz at unchanged CoreMark cyc\n…[107808 of 110880 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:994ee4a07479afb6]…\nitness\": 127.84, \"delta_pct\": -4.45, \"vs_baseline\": 954.79, \"fmax_mhz\": 53.736, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4203513, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3035, \"ff\": 717, \"seeds\": [52.002, 53.736, 53.736], \"perturbations\": [[0, 52.002, 15], [1, 53.736, 14], [2, 53.736, 14]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/result_q_23_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -14.23, \"arrival_ns\": 24.524, \"logic_cells\": 15, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 15, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T21:48:13.844238Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r11s0 (regression, -4.45%): Predecoding 17 result producers in ID/EX and using a balanced masked-OR tree left the register-file-to-EX/MEM datapath critical, so flattening result selection alone did not improve whole-core timing (53.736 MHz median) at unchanged CoreMark cycles.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
