ush still clears ID/EX.\n\nClearing every invalid decoded control is essential. hazard_unit\nreads id_ex.ctrl.mem_read without qualifying it by id_ex.valid.\nMerely clearing valid would let raw stalled imem_data create a ghost\nload dependency after fetch resumes. EX must retain its existing\nfully inert EX/MEM bubble for invalid input because memory and\nforwarding consumers are not universally valid-qualified. Keep the\ndecoder's default-illegal policy and all checks on valid encodings;\nsanitizing an invalid fetch must not legalize a valid illegal opcode.\n\nKeep current hazard priorities. Raw sou\n…[14985 of 18057 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:eada073ce2b29efe]…\nxtend tests by alternating ordinary integer, multiply, divide, JAL and JALR producers followed immediately by dependent ALU operations, branches, stores and memory-base consumers. Cover x0, faults, bubbles, long dmem holds, simultaneous imem stalls, divide completion after backpressure, reset and recovery. Check exact forwarded operands, source metadata, bank selection, results, RVFI order/PCs, and once-only retirement and stores. Keep every existing assertion and the ten-cycle progress bound. Expect unchanged CoreMark cycles. Acceptance requires median Gowin Fmax times measured iterations/cycle strictly above 139.94434, approximately 58.826 MHz at the champion's cycle count. Report measured timing honestly even if the result misses that threshold.\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_ex/u_alu > cpu/u_ex\n  full report: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261003-001-r12s0-hypgen/cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p2/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\nscore Fmax (median): 55.829 MHz\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
