{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_69", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r12s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261003-001-r12s0\ntitle: \"Flatten each four-bit divider round into parallel trial subtractions\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 133.79 at 56.239 MHz. Divider completion repeatedly\n  appears among the limiting paths: two dependent radix-4 digits precede\n  sign correction and EX/MEM capture. The earlier parallel radix-4 trial\n  subtraction change improved fitness by 11.34%, whereas custom borrow\n  prefixes and shifting work onto the launch edge regressed. Recent\n  multiplier-input and result-mux changes also regressed. Target the\n  remaining serial dependency inside the existing four-bit divider round,\n  preserving all pipeline boundaries and instruction latencies.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace only the real divider's two serial radix-4 digit networks with\n  one parallel radix-16 trial-subtraction network. This is a local\n  combinational implementation change to the same four quotient bits per\n  clock. Keep operand acceptance at edge 0, seven registered recurrence\n  updates at edges 1 through 7, and the existing final-round bypass into\n  EX/MEM at edge 8. Do not add execution states, pipeline stages, operand\n  speculation, early completion, or variable latency.\n\n  Let D be the existing unsigned divisor magnitude. Capture the divisor\n  multiples needed for 1D through 15D on the existing request edge and\n  hold them throughout the operation. Use full 36-bit unsigned multiples;\n  neither 32-bit nor the old 34-bit storage is wide enough for 15D.\n  Store D and the odd multiples 3D, 5D, 7D, 9D, 11D, 13D, 15D; obtain\n  even multiples by constant shifts of the captured odd values with\n  explicit 36-bit sizing. Generate 3D, 5D and 9D with one shifted add,\n  and 7D and 15D with (8D-D) and (16D-D). Generate 11D=8D+2D+D and\n  13D=8D+4D+D with a three-input carry-save compressor followed by one\n  carry-propagating sum, avoiding two serial wide adders at launch.\n  The compressor is S=X XOR Y XOR Z and\n  C=((X AND Y) OR (X AND Z) OR (Y AND Z)) shifted left by one;\n  the multiple is S+C. All shifts, oper\n…[4054 of 7126 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:12d7a1e776772bff]…\nges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace the two serial radix-4 digit steps with fifteen independent\n      full-width trial subtractions, adjacent-threshold one-hot digit\n      selection and balanced remainder reduction. Capture full-width odd\n      divisor multiples at request acceptance, derive even multiples by\n      wiring, and bound launch arithmetic with carry-save generation of\n      11D and 13D. Preserve all state transitions, nine-clock latency,\n      final bypass, sign correction, held completion, ALTOPS and other ops.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Add full-width multiple and radix-16 digit-boundary coverage with\n      an independent integer reference, deterministic random rounds,\n      zero divisors and signed exceptional cases. Retain original result,\n      prefix-state, exact latency, reset, operand-capture and stalled\n      completion assertions in real and ALTOPS builds; update internal\n      signal references only where the digit-network layout changes.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
