{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git status --short; git diff --check; sed -n '1,180p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r3s0.yaml\"", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261003-001-r3s0\ntitle: \"Shorten restoring-divider borrow chains with a balanced block prefix\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 93.33 at a median 41.919 MHz. Its reported worst\n  path starts at divider remainder_q[0], crosses u_alu and u_ex, and\n  reaches the timed memory logic with 28.756 ns arrival through 134 cells.\n  Four serial restoring steps, each containing a full-width subtract\n  followed by a borrow-controlled remainder mux, remain on this path.\n  LESSONS.md and log.jsonl show that reducing serial divider depth helped:\n  the six-step micro_opt reached 40.582 MHz, while the four-step champion\n  reached 41.919 MHz. The earlier fully combinational sharing attempt\n  regressed to 4.169 MHz. Target the remaining intra-step borrow dependency\n  while retaining the proven registered divider and its exact latency.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace only the unsigned trial-subtraction circuit inside each of the\n  existing four restoring steps with eight four-bit subtract blocks and\n  a balanced block-borrow prefix. This is a combinational implementation\n  change within alu.sv: retain eight rounds, acceptance at edge 0, seven\n  intermediate register updates, and final-round consumption at edge 8.\n  Keep the current sign correction, captured operands, sticky completion,\n  reset behavior, and request/consume interface. All ordinary ALU and\n  multiply operations, pipeline stages, and memory handshakes stay intact.\n\n  For each step let T = {remainder, quotient[31]} be the 33-bit unsigned\n  trial remainder and B be the captured 32-bit divisor magnitude. Split\n  T[31:0] and B into eight four-bit blocks, indexed least significant\n  first. For block i compute a five-bit zero-extended base subtraction\n  Z_i = {0,T_i} - {0,B_i}; G_i = Z_i[4] denotes borrow generation and\n  P_i = (T_i == B_i) denotes propagation of an incoming borrow. Generate\n  all block-boundary borrows with an explicit three-level parallel prefix\n  at distances 1, 2, and 4. The combine rule for a higher group H and\n  lower group L is G\n…[3202 of 6274 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c09fedfd89b00ffd]…\nse explicit widths and synthesis-compatible constant-index logic.\n      Retain all divider registers, round count, final-round sign\n      correction, immediate and held completion paths, and ALTOPS\n      formulas. Preserve every other ALU operation and the interface.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all arithmetic and exact nine-clock handshake assertions.\n      Extend real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU vectors with borrow generation and\n      propagation across every four-bit block boundary: powers of 16\n      and adjacent values, equal high blocks with differing low blocks,\n      alternating nibble patterns, long zero/f borrow runs, large\n      unsigned divisors, and dividend smaller/equal/larger cases. Check\n      all signed combinations, zero divisors, and INT_MIN/-1 against an\n      integer-only truncation-toward-zero reference. Exercise immediate\n      consumption and held final completion with changed input operands,\n      and retain existing reset, competing-request, and multiply tests.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport random\nM=(1<<32)-1\n\ndef block_sub(t,b):\n    g=[(((t>>(4*i))&15)-((b>>(4*i))&15)) < 0 for i in range(8)]\n    p=[((t>>(4*i))&15)==((b>>(4*i))&15) for i in range(8)]\n    for span in (1,2,4):\n        og,op=g,p\n        g=[og[i] or (op[i] and og[i-span]) if i>=span else og[i] for i in range(8)]\n        p=[op[i] and op[i-span] if i>=span else op[i] for i in range(8)]\n    diff=sum((((t>>(4*i))-(b>>(4*i))-(int(g[i-1]) if i else 0))&15)<<(4*i) for i in range(8))\n    borrow=not bool(t>>32) and g[7]\n    return diff, bool(borrow)\n\nrng=random.Random(0x20261003)\nvalues={0,1,M,M-1,0x80000000,0x7fffffff,0xaaaaaaaa,0x55555555,0x0f0f0f0f,0xf0f0f0f0}\nfor k in range(0,33,4):\n    for off in (-1,0,1):\n        v=(1<<k)+off\n        if 0<=v<=M: values.add(v)\ntrials=0\nfor t in sorted(values):\n    for b in sorted(values):\n        for high in (0,1):\n            tt=t+(high<<32)\n            assert block_sub(tt,b)==((tt-b)&M,tt<b)\n            trials+=1\nfor _ in range(100000):\n    t=rng.getrandbits(33); b=rng.getrandbits(32)\n    assert block_sub(t,b)==((t-b)&M,t<b)\n    trials+=1\n\ndef divide(a,b,signed,rem):\n    aa=a-(1<<32) if signed and (a>>31) else a\n    bb=b-(1<<32) if signed and (b>>31) else b\n    q=abs(aa); divisor=abs(bb); r=0\n    for _ in range(32):\n        t=(r<<1)|(q>>31)\n        diff,borrow=block_sub(t,divisor)\n        r=(t if borrow else diff)&M\n        q=((q<<1)|int(not borrow))&M\n    result=r if rem else q\n    negate=signed and (aa<0 if rem else ((aa<0)\"'!=(bb<0) and bb!=0))\n    return (-result if negate else result)&M\n\npairs=[(a,b) for a in values for b in values]\npairs.extend((rng.getrandbits(32),rng.getrandbits(32)) for _ in range(3000))\nchecks=0\nfor a,b in pairs:\n    for signed in (False,True):\n        aa=a-(1<<32) if signed and (a>>31) else a\n        bb=b-(1<<32) if signed and (b>>31) else b\n        quotient=