{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_48", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r4s0.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261003-001-r4s0\ntitle: \\\"Use validity at ID/EX instead of muxing fetched instructions to NOP\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 103.91 at 46.673 MHz. A fresh vendor placement-0\n  run reproduces 46.361 MHz, with a 26.865 ns multiplier path and an\n  almost tied 26.864 ns branch/control path. The detailed control path\n  passes from the register file through EX branch comparison, IF\n  instruction masking, a hazard source-register comparison, and ID\n  register control. IF currently replaces the entire instruction with\n  a NOP on redirect or instruction-bus stall even though IF also marks\n  that instruction invalid and ID separately flushes on redirect.\n  Removing this redundant data-path squash should shorten the control\n  path and reduce redirect fanout without adding prediction or stages.\n  Prior micro_opt borrow-prefix work regressed despite fewer cells;\n  actual Gowin timing is therefore the criterion for this local change.\nhypothesis: |\n  Carry imem_data directly in the combinational IF/ID instruction field\n  on every cycle. Keep out.valid = \"'!(flush || redirect), the existing\n  PC update, and redirect-over-stall priority. Move invalid-instruction\n  neutralization to the receiving ID/EX register: reset or explicit\n  flush clears the whole payload; otherwise a stall holds it; otherwise\n  invalid IF/ID clears the whole payload; otherwise decode and capture\n  normally. This replaces the wide instruction-to-NOP mux and its\n  redirect-dependent source addresses with narrow validity control at\n  the register boundary. It is one local bubble-insertion optimization,\n  with no changed pipeline stages, branch policy, or instruction latency.\n\n  In id_stage preserve the exact precedence with, for example:\n  if (reset || flush) reg_q <= '\"'0;\n  else if (\"'!stall && !in.valid) reg_q <= '\"'0;\n  else if (\"'!stall) capture the existing decoded fields;\n  otherwise hold. Do not clear a held instruction merely because the\n  current fetch is invalid. A dmem-stalled or divider-held instruction\n  must survive simultaneous imem backpressure. Clear every control in\n  an accepted bubble, not just valid: memory and forwarding units use\n  some controls without independently checking valid. Do not retain\n  decoded load/store/reg_write controls from an invalid raw instruction.\n\n  The hazard unit will now see raw fetched rs fields. Preserve its\n  equations and priorities. If fetch is stalled, PC already holds and\n  ID either captures an inert bubble or the load-use condition inserts\n  one. If dmem or execute waits, existing stall priority holds ID/EX.\n  On a real redirect the executing instruction is a branch or jump,\n  not a load, and the explicit ID flush wins; a raw wrong-path source\n  match cannot turn that redirect into a load-use stall. Validate these\n  interactions with directed tests instead of adding a late redirect\n  qualification to the source address bus, which recreates the path.\n\n  Preserve the decoder'\"'s illegal-by-default policy, trap behavior,\n  memory handshakes, forwarded operands, and all arithmetic including\n  exact real and ALTOPS divider schedules. Preserve nret=1 ports and\n  contiguous single-channel RVFI order. Fetched wrong-path or unready\n  instructions must never retire or cause memory/register side effects.\n  Meaningful instruction behavior and marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles\n  should remain unchanged; only invalid pipeline payloads differ.\n\n  A temporary two-file prototype passed the existing pipeline cocotb\n  runner. Gowin placement option 0 improved from 46.361 to 48.395 MHz,\n  while logic fell from 2909 to 2880 with 641 registers unchanged.\n  This is preliminary single-placement evidence, not a scored median\n  fitness result or completed formal verification. Check all three\n  vendor placement options and the actual stalled CoreMark workload.\n  Acceptance requires fitness above 108.68986; with the historical\n  4,491,485 cycles for ten iterations, this needs approximately\n  48.82 MHz. Expect about 6 percent gain, subject to placement and\n  unchanged arithmetic paths becoming critical. Run unchanged formal,\n  decoder and pipeline tests, stalled cosimulation, and canonical\n  CoreMark CRC/validation checks; never change timing brackets or gates.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Drive out.instr directly from imem_data rather than selecting a\n      NOP on flush/redirect. Preserve the current validity equation,\n      PC register, reset value, and redirect/stall priority. Update\n      comments to explain that invalid payloads are neutralized in ID.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Clear the entire ID/EX payload when accepting an invalid IF/ID\n      instruction, after reset/explicit-flush priority and below stall\n      hold priority. Preserve normal decode and capture, every register\n      field, and the existing explicit flush behavior. No other RTL\n      datapath or hazard equations need to change.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Add directed invalid-fetch and wrong-path cases whose raw bits\n      encode loads, stores, illegal instructions, and source registers\n      matching a pending load destination. Overlap imem backpressure\n      with load-use, dmem stalls, redirects, and divider waits; verify\n      held instructions survive and invalid fetches produce no memory\n      effects or retirements. Preserve all current forwarding, traps,\n      arithmetic, exact divide timing, progress, and RVFI-order checks.\n      Compare ready-bus retirement timing with the original pipeline.\n''')\nprint('Updated hypothesis to the measured validity-based bubble insertion change.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
