{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='micro_opt':\n  print('\\\\nID',d['id'],'TITLE',d['title'],'FITNESS',d['fitness'])\n  print('CRITICAL',d.get('critical_path'))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print('HYPOTHESIS',h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('NOTES',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\nID baseline-bench-683f32f TITLE Baseline retest for cores/bench FITNESS 12.12\nCRITICAL {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -189.542, 'arrival_ns': 199.837, 'logic_cells': 156, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nHYPOTHESIS \nNOTES \n\nID hyp-20261003-001-r1s0 TITLE Share and width-specialize the combinational divider FITNESS 9.28\nCRITICAL {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_1_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -243.243, 'arrival_ns': 253.537, 'logic_cells': 405, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nHYPOTHESIS Replace only the real-arithmetic DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU implementation with\none explicitly shared, fully combinational unsigned restoring divmod\nnetwork. Normalize operands to unsigned magnitudes for signed operations,\nobtain quotient and remainder from the same network, then restore the\nquotient sign from a[31] XOR b[31] and the remainder sign from a[31].\nLeave multiplication, base ALU operations, pipeline registers, forwarding,\nbus handshakes, and retirement latency unchanged. This is a local logic\noptimization, with no iterative unit, additional cycle, or timing exception.\n\nSpecialize each of the 32 unrolled steps to the number of dividend prefix\nbits processed. For step k=1..32, form the k-bit trial remainder T by\nappending dividend_magnitude[32-k] to the previous (k-1)-bit remainder;\nthe first step starts with a zero remainder. Compute a single (k+1)-bit\nzero-extended subtraction D = {0,T} - {0,divisor_magnitude[k-1:0]}.\nAccept this subtraction only when D[k] is zero and all divisor bits\nabove k-1 are zero; at k=32 the latter condition is constant true.\nThe accepted bit becomes quotient[32-k], and the next remainder is\nD[k-1:0] if accepted, otherwise T. Use elaboration-time constant widths\nand shared high-divisor prefix-OR signals. The subtraction's borrow\nsupplies the comparison as well as the candidate remainder, avoiding\nindependently described compare and subtract networks\n…[12722 of 15794 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d1d4fa7132330ff0]…\nunchanged cosimulation evaluator\npassed both available ELFs, including stalled\nselftest comparison and canonical stalled CoreMark CRC validation.\nThe unchanged CoreMark IPC evaluator measured exactly 4,491,485\nmarker-bracketed cycles for ten iterations, equal to the champion.\nThese measurements imply fitness 112.466, an 8.23 percent gain over\n103.91, exceeding the required 108.68986 acceptance threshold.\n\nExpect approximately 8 percent higher fitness. These are temporary\nprototype measurements, not a recorded tournament acceptance; the\nimplementation phase must reproduce the change and run its full\nunchanged gates. The timing benefit comes from actual removal of\ninstruction masking and control dependencies, with unchanged useful\nwork and arithmetic latency. Remaining risks are placement variation,\nanother arithmetic path becoming critical, and incorrect stall/flush\npriority when implementing invalid-payload clearing. Keep canonical\nCRCs, validation text, timing brackets, and all formal checks intact.\n\nNOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
