{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_57", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r7s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261003-001-r7s0',\n'title':'Precompute the first radix-4 digit during divider operand capture',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 133.79 at median 56.239 MHz and 4,203,513 marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its recorded worst path crosses divider completion from quotient_q[30] to EX/MEM alu_result[30], taking 24.549 ns through 80 cells. Completion currently contains two serial radix-4 digits followed by sign correction. Prior borrow-prefix arithmetic regressed through routing overhead, and proposal-stage experiments with speculative sign correction also regressed. Target the amount of arithmetic on the completion edge while preserving the current external latency and ordinary two-digit recurrence.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Compute the first radix-4 quotient digit on the existing operand-capture edge, using a small exact predecode of the dividend's top two magnitude bits and the divisor magnitude. Keep the existing seven intermediate clocks of two radix-4 digits each, then use only the first digit of the existing two-digit network for final completion. The total is 1 + 7*2 + 1 = 16 radix-4 digits. Acceptance remains edge 0, intermediate updates remain edges 1 through 7, availability still asserts before edge 8, and direct consumption still occurs at edge 8. This is one local optimization of divider launch/completion arithmetic, with no new pipeline stage, state register, bus protocol, or instruction cycle.\n\nLet A and D be the same unsigned magnitudes already used by the divider, and P=A[31:30]. Since 0 <= P <= 3, compute the initial quotient digit q0 and remainder r0 using only these cases: D=0 gives q0=3,r0=P; D=1 gives q0=P,r0=0; D=2 gives q0={0,P[1]},r0={0,P[0]}; D=3 gives q0=(P==3),r0=(P==3 ? 0 : P); every D>=4 gives q0=0,r0=P. Use explicitly sized unsigned expressions and full-width divisor equality tests, or an equivalent shared high-bit-zero guard plus low-bit decode. Do not truncate D before deciding whether it exceeds three. Share the existing signed-magnitude normalization.\n\nOn accepted div_request initialize quotient_q to {A[29:0],q0} and remainder_q to the zero-extended r0. Capture divisor_q, divisor3_q, negate_q, and remainder_op_q exactly as before. Preserve the existing round counter, IDLE/ROUND/DONE transitions, busy/valid logic, reset priority, operand capture, and completion storage. In the seven non-final rounds continue registering digit_quotient[2] and digit_remainder[2]. For final_result only, select digit_quotient[1] or digit_remainder[1] using remainder_op_q, then apply the existing conditional sign correction. Do not change quotient_next/remainder_next globally to one-digit results: the intermediate rounds must still process four bits each. The unused second digit on the final round may evaluate but must not affect completion.\n\nAfter operand capture two dividend bits have been processed. After intermediate edge e=1..7, exactly 2+4*e bits have been processed; before completion 30 bits are done and one radix-4 digit completes all 32. For each registered boundary, compare quotient and remainder to independent integer division of that consumed dividend prefix. For a zero divisor the consumed quotient prefix is all ones and the remainder is the consumed dividend prefix. These invariants validate both the launch predecode and the shifted recurrence schedule.\n\nKeep signed truncation toward zero, dividend-signed remainder, zero-divisor results, quotient sign suppression for zero divisor, and INT_MIN/-1 behavior. Keep all RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS formulas and their exact existing handshake schedule. Preserve forwarded-operand metadata capture, stalled completion, immediate dependent consumers, all top-level nret=1 ports, RVFI order, decoder legality, memory handshakes, and all correctness/progress gates. No changes to EX, forwarding, prediction, register-file mapping, or the multiplier are part of this proposal.\n\nExpect approximately 8 percent higher fitness at unchanged CoreMark cycles. Acceptance requires fitness strictly above 139.94434, or approximately 58.83 MHz at the champion's measured cycle count. This is a hypothesis, not an accepted result. The timing benefit is removing one wide subtract/borrow/select layer from the completion-to-EX/MEM path without increasing the depth of the recurring two-digit path. The capture predecode is narrow, but magnitude normalization followed by its divisor-zero/small-divisor tests could become critical. Recurrence, multiplication, branch recovery, and placement sensitivity remain risks.\n\nRun the real and ALTOPS ALU suites with their original external latency/reset/backpressure assertions intact. Update only the internal prefix-state expectations to reflect the intentional initial two-bit step, and add focused D=0,1,2,3,4 tests for each possible P and all operand signs, including INT_MIN. Preserve every existing assertion's arithmetic meaning. Run unchanged pipeline/formal/liveness checks, stalled retirement cosim, and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation. Measure all three Gowin placement options and actual marker-bracketed cycles; do not infer a fitness win from fewer logic cells. ALTOPS alone does not prove real arithmetic, so also validate the new launch step exhaustively over its small P/D equivalence classes and retain actual-arithmetic recurrence tests.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'Precompute the exact first radix-4 digit during operand capture with the D=0/1/2/3/>=4 cases. Initialize shifted quotient and two-bit remainder accordingly. Retain seven two-digit intermediate updates, and source final sign correction from digit_quotient[1]/digit_remainder[1]. Preserve all divider control, latency, exceptional semantics, ALTOPS, and other ALU operations.'},\n {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Retain all real/ALTOPS result, nine-clock schedule, reset, operand-capture, and held-completion assertions. Adjust internal quotient/remainder checks to two consumed bits at acceptance and 2+4*e bits after intermediate edge e. Add exhaustive launch-prefix classes with divisors 0 through 4, large divisors, signed magnitudes, and integer-reference full DIV/REM results.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final-angle hypothesis written and schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
