memory bounds and MMIO timing brackets. Run the\n  unchanged arithmetic suites as part of the implementation gates.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: |\n      Split the array into two native 16x32 distributed-RAM banks.\n      Preserve synchronous reset and write behavior. Merge bank selection,\n      x0 masking and write-first bypass into a parallel three-source read\n      reduction independently for both ports, with mutually exclusive masks.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Connect register-file reads to raw fetch source fields, remove the\n      unused address wires and explicitly disconnect ID address outputs.\n      Preserve masked instruction delivery, validity and all pipeline wiring.\n  - file: test/test_reg_file.py\n    description: |\n      Cover both banks, all source/destination address pairs, x15/x16,\n      x0, reset after writes, and same-cycle write-first behavior on\n      either and both read ports using an independent register model.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise raw source fields during invalid fetches, recovery,\n      load-use, dmem holds and divider waits. Retain exact RVFI operands,\n      order, memory effects, forwarding and progress assertions.\n''')\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert h['id']=='hyp-20261003-001-r9s0' and h['category']=='micro_opt'\nassert type(h['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nassert -50 <= h['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct'] <= 50\nprint('Final hypothesis written; schema validation passed.')\nPY\ngit status --short\"", "aggregated_output": "Final hypothesis written; schema validation passed.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
