{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_15", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nbase=4203513; dep=35640; threshold=133.79*1.046\nprint('Nominal_added_cycles_pct',100*dep/base)\nprint('Fmax_for_acceptance_MHz_if_unhidden',threshold*(base+dep)/1e7)\nprint('Fmax_for_12pct_fitness_MHz_if_unhidden',133.79*1.12*(base+dep)/1e7)\nPY\nsed -n '1,175p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r10s1.yaml\ngit status --short --untracked-files=all\"", "aggregated_output": "Nominal_added_cycles_pct 0.8478622523589198\nFmax_for_acceptance_MHz_if_unhidden 59.32454687440201\nFmax_for_12pct_fitness_MHz_if_unhidden 63.521503345439996\nid: hyp-20261003-002-r10s1\ntitle: \"Pipeline M-extension completion across the existing EX/MEM boundary\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 133.79 at 56.239 MHz and 4,203,513 bracketed\n  CoreMark cycles. Recent structural attempts show competing arithmetic\n  limits: r8s1 result banking left divider completion critical, while\n  r9s1 removed divider-origin worst paths but exposed the register-file\n  through multiplier path and regressed 6.58 percent. Rearranging only\n  result muxes or only divider capture has not cleared the acceptance\n  margin. MEM currently transports an already finished M-extension result;\n  use that existing pipeline interval to finish arithmetic instead.\nhypothesis: |\n  Retiming M-extension execution across the existing EX/MEM boundary is\n  the single structural change. Make MUL/MULH/MULHSU/MULHU and completed\n  DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU late-result producers, like loads: EX/MEM transports\n  registered partial arithmetic and MEM completes it into MEM/WB. Keep\n  ordinary integer execution, branch resolution, the predictor, the\n  independent effective-address register, memory transactions, pipeline\n  depth and single retirement port. This is a true arithmetic register\n  boundary, not parallel banks containing already completed results.\n\n  For multiplication, replace the three full-width combinational products\n  with four parallel 16-bit-limb partial products. Treat each low limb as\n  positive signed 17-bit {0, operand[15:0]}. Treat each high limb as signed\n  17-bit {signed_operand && operand[31], operand[31:16]}; signed_operand\n  is true for both operands on MULH, only rs1 on MULHSU, and neither on\n  MULHU or MUL. Compute the four signed 34-bit limb products from the\n  exact forwarded operands and register them at EX/MEM with the selected\n  operation and metadata. In MEM, sign-extend each product to 64 bits,\n  shift the two cross\n…[7712 of 10784 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e149553ad98b22c4]…\nface and RVFI mapping.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Generalize the load-use condition to loads and all M-result\n      producers, adding exactly one dependency bubble after their EX\n      advance while preserving divider-wait, dmem-hold and recovery\n      priorities. Partial EX/MEM arithmetic must never be forwarded.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all exact M arithmetic vectors and handshake assertions while\n      exercising the new split arithmetic boundary, using a composed test\n      top under rtl if needed. Check partial reconstruction, 30-bit-prefix\n      divider state, completion retention, reset and real/ALTOPS schedules.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Add M late-result dependency and throughput cases, including\n      back-to-back multiply/divide consumers, branches, stores, address\n      bases, x0, competing destinations, faults and bus stalls. Preserve\n      all existing architectural assertions and liveness bounds; verify\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
