{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|hyp-20261003-002-r(9|10|11)s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move division into a bounded multicycle execute unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline scores 12.12 with median Fmax 5.442 MHz. Its reported worst\\npath is 199.837 ns across 156 cells through forwarding and the execute\\nALU. alu.sv implements signed and unsigned division and remainder with\\ncombinational / and % operators, making these the strongest suspected\\nsource of the deep arithmetic path even when ordinary instructions run.\\nThe history contains only the baseline and no prior structural attempt;\\nLESSONS.md is absent. Separating division from the ordinary execute path\\nshould trade a few cycles per divide for a substantially faster clock\\nacross the complete CoreMark run.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline scores 12.12 with median Fmax 5.442 MHz. Its reported worst\\npath is 199.837 ns across 156 cells through forwarding and the execute\\nALU. alu.sv implements signed and unsigned division and remainder with\\ncombinational / and % operators, making these the strongest suspected\\nsource of the deep arithmetic path even when ordinary instructions run.\\nThe history contains only the baseline and no prior structural attempt;\\nLESSONS.md is absent. Separating division from the ordinary execute path\\nshould trade a few cycles per divide for a substantially faster clock\\nacross the complete CoreMark run.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU execution with one shared, registered,\\nblocking divider. Capture the post-forwarding operands and operation\\nonce, prepare unsigned magnitudes, perform eight radix-2 restoring\\nquotient-bit steps per clock for four clocks, and register the signed\\nquotient or remainder before transferring the instruction to EX/MEM.\\nEach restoring step uses one extended subtract and its borrow to select\\nthe next remainder. Separate magnitude preparation and sign correction\\nfrom the four arithmetic rounds: accept and latch magnitudes at edge 0,\\nrun rounds at edges 1 through 4, register the corrected res\n…[130062 of 133134 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:25549e0bd1b435e5]…\n82, \"delta_pct\": 3.01, \"vs_baseline\": 1037.13, \"fmax_mhz\": 54.956, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3987564, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3266, \"ff\": 833, \"seeds\": [53.458, 54.956, 54.956], \"perturbations\": [[0, 53.458, 23], [1, 54.956, 22], [2, 54.956, 22]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_2_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_29_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -13.706, \"arrival_ns\": 24.001, \"logic_cells\": 73, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 23, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T21:43:48.307915Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r11s1 (regression, +3.01%): A two-entry fall-through fetch queue cut measured CoreMark cycles by 5.14% through bus-stall overlap, but unchanged divider-completion and register-file/multiplier paths limited median Fmax to 54.956 MHz, leaving the net gain below the 4.6% acceptance margin.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
