{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|hyp-20261003-002-r1s1|divider|liveness' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Share and width-specialize the combinational divider\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline achieves 12.12 CoreMark iterations/second at 5.442 MHz.\\nIts reported worst path crosses forwarding and the combinational ALU,\\ntaking 199.837 ns through 156 cells. The four signed/unsigned division\\nand remainder expressions are the strongest RTL-level suspect for this\\ndepth, although the available path summary does not identify individual\\narithmetic cells. This path limits every cycle, even when no divide is\\nexecuting. There are no earlier non-baseline attempts in the local log.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline achieves 12.12 CoreMark iterations/second at 5.442 MHz.\\nIts reported worst path crosses forwarding and the combinational ALU,\\ntaking 199.837 ns through 156 cells. The four signed/unsigned division\\nand remainder expressions are the strongest RTL-level suspect for this\\ndepth, although the available path summary does not identify individual\\narithmetic cells. This path limits every cycle, even when no divide is\\nexecuting. There are no earlier non-baseline attempts in the local log.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the real-arithmetic DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU implementation with\\none explicitly shared, fully combinational unsigned restoring divmod\\nnetwork. Normalize operands to unsigned magnitudes for signed operations,\\nobtain quotient and remainder from the same network, then restore the\\nquotient sign from a[31] XOR b[31] and the remainder sign from a[31].\\nLeave multiplication, base ALU operations, pipeline registers, forwarding,\\nbus handshakes, and retirement latency unchanged. This is a local logic\\noptimization, with no iterative unit, additional cycle, or timing exception.\\n\\nSpecialize each of the 32 unrolled steps to the number of dividend prefix\\nbits processed. For step k=1..32, form the k-bit trial remainder T by\\nappending dividend_magnitude[32-k] to the previous (k-1)-bit remainder;\\nthe first step starts with a zero remainder. \n…[15365 of 18437 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b3d476b4531f9442]…\nates.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 71.56, \"delta_pct\": 490.43, \"vs_baseline\": 490.43, \"fmax_mhz\": 32.14, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2904, \"ff\": 607, \"seeds\": [31.502, 32.14, 32.14], \"perturbations\": [[0, 31.502, 49], [1, 32.14, 47], [2, 32.14, 47]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_31_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_0_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -26.744, \"arrival_ns\": 37.038, \"logic_cells\": 262, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 49, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T16:04:38.415320Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r1s1 (improvement, +490.43%): Replacing combinational `/` and `%` in `alu.sv` with a registered divider limited to eight restoring steps per cycle shortened the clock-limiting arithmetic path enough to outweigh seven-clock DIV/REM latency in CoreMark.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
