{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='structural':\n  print(json.dumps({k:d.get(k) for k in ['id','title','fitness','fmax_mhz','cycles','critical_path','implementation_notes']},indent=2))\n  if d['id'].endswith('r3s1'):\n   print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261003-002-r1s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Move division into a bounded multicycle execute unit\",\n  \"fitness\": 71.56,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 32.14,\n  \"cycles\": 4491485,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_31_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_0_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -26.744,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 37.038,\n    \"logic_cells\": 262,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\"\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261003-002-r2s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Retiming division to four restoring steps with fused completion\",\n  \"fitness\": 93.33,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 41.919,\n  \"cycles\": 4491485,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_0_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -18.461,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 28.756,\n    \"logic_cells\": 134,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\"\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261003-002-r3s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Replace the restoring divider chain with parallel radix-4 digit selection\",\n  \"fitness\": 103.91,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 46.673,\n  \"cycles\": 4491485,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\",\n    \"to\": \"dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -16.57,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 26.865,\n    \"logic_cells\": 14,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\"\n}\nReplace the divider's four serial radix-2 restoring steps per clock\nwith two serial radix-4 restoring digits. Each radix-4 digit chooses\ntwo quotient bits by computing trial remainders for D, 2D, and 3D\nin parallel, then selecting the largest nonnegative subtraction.\nThis is a single structural change to the divider datapath topology:\nparallel trial arithmetic replaces serial bit-by-bit decisions.\nReuse the current eight-round controller, operand capture, fused\ncompletion boundary, and blocking execute handshake. Ordinary ALU\nand multiply operations retain their current paths and latency.\n\nAt acceptance e\n…[3251 of 6323 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b7ffa8e248e34e11]…\nfor consecutive divides.\nA proposal-stage Python model of these two radix-4 digits per round\nmatched 82,992 DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU reference results from directed and\nseeded-random inputs, including checks on intermediate width and\nremainder bounds. This validates the proposed arithmetic recurrence,\nnot an RTL implementation, formal proof, or FPGA timing result.\n\nPredict a 25 percent fitness improvement from fewer serial carry\nchains, with unchanged instruction timing and little area pressure\nrelative to the 10,000-LUT target. This is an estimate, not a timing\nmeasurement. Acceptance requires median Gowin Fmax times measured\nbracketed iterations/cycle greater than 97.62318, which is 4.6 percent\nabove 93.33. At 4,491,485 cycles for ten iterations this requires\napproximately 43.85 MHz. The principal risks are wider parallel\nsubtractors and selection routing erasing the depth gain, the new\nmagnitude-to-3D capture path, final sign correction, or another\nexisting path becoming critical. Judge the complete timed core.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
