{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md schemas/hypothesis.schema.json'", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r1s1 (improvement, +490.43%): Replacing combinational `/` and `%` in `alu.sv` with a registered divider limited to eight restoring steps per cycle shortened the clock-limiting arithmetic path enough to outweigh seven-clock DIV/REM latency in CoreMark.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r1s2 (regression, +7.01%): A 128-entry bimodal predictor plus direct-JAL prediction cut CoreMark cycles by 6.4% by removing redirect bubbles, but the unchanged forwarding/combinational-ALU critical path kept Fmax near 5.45 MHz, limiting the fitness gain over baseline to 7%.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r2s1 (improvement, +30.42%): Halving the divider's restoring recurrence from eight steps to four and fusing final-round sign correction into EX/MEM let reduced arithmetic depth outweigh the increase from seven to nine blocking DIV/REM clocks in CoreMark.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r2s2 (regression, +4.74%): Adding a 128-entry bimodal/JAL predictor cut CoreMark cycles by 6.4% but lowered median Fmax from 32.14 to 31.494 MHz with the unchanged divider still critical, showing that fetch-side additions can consume timing margin in unrelated arithmetic paths.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r3s0 (regression, -28.15%): Balanced four-bit borrow prefixes in `alu.sv` reduced critical-path cell count but left four restoring steps serial with routing dominating delay (~60%), lowering Gowin median Fmax from 41.919 to 30.118 MHz at unchanged CoreMark cycles; fewer arithmetic cells do not guarantee faster FPGA timing.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r3s1 (improvement, +11.34%): Parallel D/2D/3D trial subtraction with registered 3D and one-hot selection in `alu.sv` shortened each divider round from four dependent radix-2 steps to two radix-4 digits, improving fitness without increasing the nine-clock DIV/REM latency.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r4s0 (regression, +8.24%): Removing the IF instruction-to-NOP mux shortened the redirect-to-hazard control path and raised median Gowin Fmax to 50.514 MHz at unchanged CoreMark cycles; accepted invalid fetches must clear the entire ID/EX payload because downstream controls are not uniformly gated by valid, while stalls must preserve held instructions.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r4s2 (improvement, +8.92%): Learning agreement with the branch displacement sign lets oppositely biased branches reinforce shared counters, enabling a 16-entry table with local updates and an MSB-only lookup plus direct-JAL prediction to deliver a net CoreMark fitness gain.\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
