ules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, \"error\": null}\nPROPOSAL: Replace only DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU execution with one shared, registered,\nblocking divider. Capture the post-forwarding operands and operation\nonce, prepare unsigned magnitudes, perform eight radix-2 restoring\nquotient-bit steps per clock for four clocks, and register the signed\nquotient or remainder before transferring the instruction to EX/MEM.\nEach restoring step uses one extended subtract and its borrow to select\nthe next remainder. Separate magnitude preparation and sign correction\nfrom the four arithmetic rounds: accept and latch magnitudes at edge 0,\nrun rounds at edges 1 through 4, register the corrected result at edge 5,\nand transfer it to EX/MEM at edge 6. Bound execution to these seven EX\nclocks including request c\n…[19624 of 22696 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ac379aff7e3d2e0e]…\n divides;\ncoincident imem/dmem stalls; load-use aliases; divider holds; and\nreset. Invalid fetches must never retire, launch division, write a\nregister, or cause a memory access. Compare valid retirement records\nand cycle traces against the champion under identical ready streams.\nRun existing unit, formal, stalled cosim, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART,\nand marker checks without changing their contracts. Main risks are\nincomplete invalid-control sanitization and remaining multiplier or\ndivider paths limiting the clock below the acceptance threshold.\n\nNOTES: \n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-003-r4s2\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"title\": \"Sixteen-entry agree prediction with instruction-derived branch bias\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 113.18, \"fmax_mhz\": 47.574, \"cycles\": 4203513, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -16.512, \"arrival_ns\": 26.807, \"logic_cells\": 16, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"error\": null}\n", "exi