{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_47", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r7s1.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261003-002-r7s1',\n'title':'Replace the inferred register RAM with flop words and balanced reads',\n'category':'structural',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 133.79 at median 56.239 MHz with 4,203,513 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Multiple recent timing reports expose a register-file read path through operand capture and execute arithmetic or recovery control. The r6s0 distributed-RAM attempt improved its parent by 4.49 percent but missed acceptance and retained a memory-based read structure. The champion's registered forwarding decisions remove comparator depth from EX, making the remaining register-file storage/read boundary a useful structural target. Current area is only 3,118 LUTs and 701 registers, leaving room to exchange storage density for a shorter clock path.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace the inferred 32x32 register-file memory with 31 independently instantiated 32-bit flip-flop words, shared by two explicitly balanced combinational read trees. Implement x0 as a constant zero leaf rather than storage. This is one structural storage-and-read topology change inside reg_file.sv. Preserve the module interface, pipeline depth, all instruction acceptance and retirement cycles, and the current reset, write-first bypass, and x0 semantics.\n\nUse a generate block for each architectural word 1 through 31. Each block owns its own local 32-bit value_q register and synchronous always_ff process: reset clears that word; otherwise an enabled write whose address equals the word index captures w_data. Do not declare a dynamically written packed memory array or force a vendor RAM primitive. The purpose is to make the architectural state explicit flops and retain the existing ID/EX operand-register boundary rather than allow a synchronous-memory implementation to absorb it. Confirm the actual mapping in the Gowin reports; source-level naming alone is not evidence of the intended circuit.\n\nFor each read port, decode its five-bit source address into one word select per nonzero register. Gate each word's 32-bit value with that select, use a zero leaf for x0, and reduce the 32 leaves through an explicit five-level balanced binary OR tree. Only the selected word contributes. Keep the existing final write-first bypass and x0 priority: a read of zero returns zero even during a write to zero; an enabled matching nonzero WB write returns w_data in the same cycle; otherwise use the read-tree result. Preserve reset-before-write priority and every architectural register's zero reset state. Do not change read addresses, add a new clock or read latency, or alter ID/EX hold/flush behavior.\n\nThe intended benefit is to replace the timing-sensitive inferred memory read and control path with ordinary flops and shallow logic, giving placement more freedom while preserving throughput. Extra flops, decode fanout, reset/write distribution, and read-tree routing are the principal costs. This does not presume that more flops are always faster: measure the complete circuit across all three Gowin placement options. Existing multiply/divider and recovery paths may cap the gain.\n\nPreserve nret=1, all external ports, contiguous channel-0 retirement, decoder legality, traps, both bus handshakes, exact real and ALTOPS arithmetic, independent effective-address capture, the champion's registered forwarding selectors, and the ten-cycle ready-bus progress bound. Run existing register-file and pipeline tests, unchanged formal, stalled retirement cosim, and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/MMIO-bracket checks. Check all 31 writable registers, both simultaneous reads, zero reads/writes, same-cycle WB bypass, reset/write overlap, consecutive writes, and dependencies across long dmem holds and imem gaps. Expect unchanged CoreMark cycles; do not weaken any checks to accept altered initialization or operand capture.\n\nAcceptance requires median Gowin Fmax times measured iterations/cycle strictly above 139.94434, approximately 58.828 MHz at the champion's cycle count. The expected gain is an estimate pending complete timing and correctness validation. Keep the change confined to this register-file topology rather than combining unrelated divider or predictor changes.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':12,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/reg_file.sv','description':'''Replace dynamically indexed register storage with independent generated flop words for x1-x31, local decoded write enables, and constant x0. Build one balanced masked-OR read tree per port. Retain synchronous zero reset, existing final write-first bypass, x0 priority, interface, and zero added read latency.\\\\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_reg_file.py','description':'''Retain every current assertion and verify all architectural words through both ports, independent simultaneous reads, matching/nonmatching writes, write-first bypass, x0 immunity, reset/write overlap, and repeated writes. Require identical zero-reset behavior.\\\\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Keep all existing architectural, forwarding, memory, and progress assertions. Exercise WB-to-decode reads and dependencies spanning load-use bubbles, division, recovery, and prolonged memory holds, comparing exact RVFI sources, results, order, and once-only retirement.\\\\n'''}]}\nclass D(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef strings(dumper,data): return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',data,style='|' if '\\\\n' in data else None)\nD.add_representer(str,strings)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(h,Dumper=D,sort_keys=False,width=84))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Wrote and validated register-file structural hypothesis')\nPY\ncat cores/bench/generated/hypgen-r7s1/floprf-timing.log\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
