{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_2", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git status --short && rg -n 'predictor|r[1-9]s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Instruction-aware bimodal prediction for the fused fetch/decode stage\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline always fetches PC+4 and redirects on every taken conditional\\nbranch and every jump. Despite the five-stage description, IF/ID is a\\ncombinational bundle, so each such redirect discards one younger fetch/decode\\nslot. CoreMark's repeated loops and calls offer an opportunity to eliminate\\nthose bubbles. The only recorded experiment is the 12.12 baseline; there is\\nno LESSONS.md or prior predictor result. Its measured worst path runs through\\nforwarding and the combinational ALU, so this proposal targets iterations\\nper cycle while keeping predictor logic out of that arithmetic path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline always fetches PC+4 and redirects on every taken conditional\\nbranch and every jump. Despite the five-stage description, IF/ID is a\\ncombinational bundle, so each such redirect discards one younger fetch/decode\\nslot. CoreMark's repeated loops and calls offer an opportunity to eliminate\\nthose bubbles. The only recorded experiment is the 12.12 baseline; there is\\nno LESSONS.md or prior predictor result. Its measured worst path runs through\\nforwarding and the combinational ALU, so this proposal targets iterations\\nper cycle while keeping predictor logic out of that arithmetic path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add one instruction-aware next-PC predictor to the existing fused IF/ID\\nstage: a 128-entry table of two-bit saturating conditional-branch counters,\\nindexed by fetch PC[8:2], combined with immediate targets from the current\\ninstruction. Initialize counters to weakly not taken (01). Predict a legal\\nconditional branch taken when its counter MSB is one, and predict legal\\ndirect JAL instructions taken unconditionally. Reconstruct the signed B/J\\nimmediate and add it to the current full 32-bit PC. All other instructions,\\nincluding JALR, predict PC+4. Check the BRANCH funct3 and target alignment\\nbefore speculating; reserved enc\n…[190837 of 193909 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2d1551fde1d7ff99]…\n \"delta_pct\": 0.61, \"vs_baseline\": 1010.64, \"fmax_mhz\": 56.584, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4203513, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3063, \"ff\": 702, \"seeds\": [53.83, 56.584, 56.584], \"perturbations\": [[0, 53.83, 22], [1, 56.584, 21], [2, 56.584, 21]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_30_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_16_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -13.577, \"arrival_ns\": 23.871, \"logic_cells\": 78, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 22, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T20:30:12.027278Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r9s2 (regression, +0.61%): Folding prediction polarity into ID/EX `miss_branch_op` and prequalifying direct-target alignment simplifies EX recovery without reducing CoreMark cycles, but competing multiplier/divider and register-file timing paths keep the gain below the 4.6% acceptance margin.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
