{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_43", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r12s2.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261003-003-r12s2\ntitle: \\\"Confine immediate prediction squash to ID/EX controls\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Predictor recovery currently masks every fetched instruction bit to NOP\n  and clears every ID/EX data field. This puts the forwarded EX branch\n  decision upstream of register-file read addresses, decode data, and many\n  register clear controls. Prior hyp-20261003-001-r4s0 showed that removing\n  instruction masking can improve timing, but still cleared the entire\n  ID/EX bundle. The separate EX kill in r6s2 moved annulment downstream;\n  r10s2 and r11s2 added recovery state and failed to improve the champion.\n  Test a distinct predictor recovery boundary: preserve immediate PC repair\n  and squash in ID/EX, restricting squash to side-effect controls and\n  prediction validity while keeping instruction and operand data independent.\nhypothesis: |\n  Implement one change to prediction recovery: separate ID/EX control\n  annulment from ID/EX data capture. Keep the existing sixteen local two-bit\n  agreement counters, direct JAL prediction, target additions, prediction\n  metadata, and direction-XOR EX recovery. Add no target cache, prediction\n  table, kill register, pipeline stage, or recovery cycle.\n\n  IF always emits raw imem_data as out.instr. Preserve out.valid =\n  \"'!(flush || redirect) and the existing predicted_taken qualification.\n  Preserve reset then accepted EX redirect then ordinary accepted prediction\n  as PC priorities. The EX miss signal repairs PC at the same edge and\n  invalidates the younger slot, but no longer selects a NOP on instruction\n  bits driving decode and register-file addresses. Predictor lookup and the\n  existing hazard/forwarding comparisons continue using the raw instruction.\n  Keep all hazard equations and priorities unchanged.\n\n  Split the ID/EX register into two update domains without changing its\n  bundle type. The data domain contains pc, rs1_val, rs2_val, imm, rd,\n  rs1_addr, rs2_addr, both forwarding selectors, and instr. Reset clears\n  those fields; otherwise capture their ordinary decoded/raw values exactly\n  when !stall, independently of flush and in.valid; otherwise hold them.\n  Neither recovery nor unavailable-fetch validity clears or masks data.\n  Data may be captured during a recovery bubble, or retained during a\n  simultaneous load-use stall and explicit flush. It remains inert.\n\n  The control domain contains the ENTIRE ctrl_t, valid, and predicted_taken.\n  Its priority is reset, explicit flush, hold, then capture. Reset or flush\n  clears all three fields. If stalled without flush, retain them even if\n  the current fetch is invalid. Otherwise valid captures in.valid;\n  predicted_taken captures in.valid && in.predicted_taken; ctrl captures\n  ctrl_decoded when in.valid, and all zero otherwise. Never clear only valid:\n  downstream memory and some forwarding consumers do not independently\n  qualify every control. Do not mask live decoded data or register-file\n  addresses with recovery.\n\n  On a miss EX advances the resolving transfer, PC immediately takes the\n  architectural successor, and ID/EX receives inert controls at that same\n  edge. The younger raw data may reside in ID/EX but cannot issue a memory\n  transaction, write a register, launch division, train prediction, redirect,\n  or retire. EX'\"'s existing \"'!in.valid bubble path remains intact. This loses\n  exactly the existing one execute slot; correct predictions retain their\n  younger instruction. Do not introduce delayed EX annulment or alter the\n  independent EX/MEM effective-address register'\"'s capture schedule. Harmless\n  sums from invalid slots have zero memory controls.\n\n  Preserve complete ID/EX holds during dmem and divide waits, the load-use\n  control bubble, MEM/WB forwarding-data retention, and recovery priority\n  over imem backpressure on memory release. Hold selectors with their data\n  on a real stall; selectors need not become zero in an invalid bubble.\n  Prediction lookup and captured prediction must agree at acceptance.\n  Train exactly once per advancing legal non-faulting branch under the\n  existing conditions. Preserve decoder legality, traps, architectural\n  RVFI next PC and link values, contiguous order, nret=1, both memory\n  handshakes, real/ALTOPS arithmetic, and the unchanged maximum ten-clock\n  ready-bus retirement gap. Modify no correctness or timing contract.\n\n  A temporary prototype of this exact control-only ID/EX squash measured\n  Gowin placement frequencies 49.548, 53.274, and 53.274 MHz, median 53.274 MHz.\n  Option-zero usage was 3,129 logic cells, 701 registers, eight LUT RAMs,\n  six BSRAMs, and six DSPs. The existing pipeline cocotb runner passed.\n  These are proposal-stage measurements, not tournament acceptance. The\n  intended mechanism did not remove the remaining register-file to EX/MEM\n  arithmetic and divider-completion bottlenecks. At unchanged champion\n  cycles this projects about 126.74 fitness, approximately 5.3 percent BELOW\n  133.79. Expected impact is therefore -5 percent with low confidence in\n  improvement; this candidate is not an observed speedup.\n\n  Rerun all unchanged formal and stalled cosim gates, canonical CoreMark\n  CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation, and the scored Gowin median during\n  implementation. Acceptance requires fitness strictly above 139.94434;\n  at 4,203,513 bracketed cycles for ten iterations it requires median Fmax\n  above approximately 58.826 MHz. Do not relax correctness or progress\n  checks. Restore temporary prototype RTL after research; this YAML is\n  the sole proposal deliverable.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: -5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Emit raw imem_data in out.instr through recovery and bus stalls.\n      Retain existing validity/prediction qualification, agreement table\n      and training, direct target logic, and immediate redirect-over-stall\n      PC priority. Update stale instruction-masking comments.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Separate reset/hold/data capture from control/prediction annulment.\n      Data including forwarding selectors captures on \"'!stall with no\n      flush/valid-dependent clearing. Entire ctrl_t, valid, and\n      predicted_taken clear on reset/flush; otherwise hold on stall or\n      capture inert controls for an invalid accepted fetch. Keep the\n      bundle layout, legal instruction semantics, and decoder unchanged.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check both ID/EX update domains, raw wrong-path instructions, and\n      nonzero data in inert bubbles. Model selector capture/hold separately\n      from control flush while retaining all live forwarding assertions.\n      Check one lost slot per miss, once-only training, imem-stalled repair,\n      dmem-release and load-use/divide holds, unchanged ten-clock progress,\n      architectural PC/link/order, and no wrong-path memory/divider/register\n      effects. Preserve all existing architectural and progress assertions.\n  - file: test/test_if_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Assert out.instr equals raw imem_data during flush, redirect, and holds;\n      retain the independent agreement-counter and acceptance-edge model.\n      Check recovery still clears validity and predicted_taken and has\n      priority over every fetch hold.\nYAML\npython3 - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np='cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r12s2.yaml'\nd=yaml.safe_load(open(p));jsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Schema valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
