serve the exact precedence with, for example:\nif (reset || flush) reg_q <= '0;\nelse if (!stall && !in.valid) reg_q <= '0;\nelse if (!stall) capture the existing decoded fields;\notherwise hold. Do not clear a held instruction merely because the\ncurrent fetch is invalid. A dmem-stalled or divider-held instruction\nmust survive simultaneous imem backpressure. Clear every control in\nan accepted bubble, not just valid: memory and forwarding units use\nsome controls without independently checking valid. Do not retain\ndecoded load/store/reg_write controls from an invalid raw instruction.\n\nThe hazard unit will now see raw fetched rs fields. Preserve its\nequations and priorities. If fetch is stalled, PC already holds and\nID either captures an inert bubble or the \n…[10576 of 13648 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8d56b35b3151020d]…\n    : {{20{imem_data[31]}}, imem_data[7], imem_data[30:25],\n                  imem_data[11:8], 1'b0};\n    direct_target = pc + direct_imm;\n    predicted_taken = (direct_jump ||\n                       (legal_branch && (imem_data[31] == agree_msb[pc[5:2]])))\n                    && direct_target[1:0] == 2'b00;\n    next_pc = predicted_taken ? direct_target : pc + 32'd4;\n  end\n\n  // EX only recovers on advance, so dmem holds cannot lose a recovery.\n  // On release it overrides imem backpressure and kills the younger slot.\n  // Otherwise PC and ID/EX accept the same live lookup at the same edge.\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if      (reset)    pc <= RESET_PC;\n    else if (redirect) pc <= redirect_target;\n    else if (!stall)   pc <= next_pc;\n  end\n\n  assign imem_addr = pc;\n\n  always_comb begin\n    out.pc    = pc;\n    out.instr = (flush || redirect) ? 32'h0000_0013 : imem_data;\n    out.predicted_taken = predicted_taken && !(reset || flush || redirect);\n    out.valid = !(flush || redirect);\n  end\n\nendmodule\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
