{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' Makefile; cat cores/bench/test/conftest.py; sed -n '1,180p' cores/bench/test/_helpers.py; rg -n '\"'^def test|''^async def test|runner|__main__'\"' cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py; rg -n 'def main|argparse|add_argument|def run' tools/eval/gowin.py tools/eval/timing.py tools/eval/fpga.py\"", "aggregated_output": ".PHONY: help lint test test-infra cosim formal fpga timing next loop report bench clean\n.DEFAULT_GOAL := help\n\n# Resolve OSS CAD Suite path so commands work even when the user hasn't\n# sourced .toolchain/oss-cad-suite/environment in this shell.\nTOOLCHAIN_DIR := $(CURDIR)/.toolchain\nOSS_BIN       := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/oss-cad-suite/bin\nLOCAL_BIN     := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/bin\nexport PATH := $(OSS_BIN):$(LOCAL_BIN):$(PATH)\n\n# Orchestrator knobs (pass-through to tools.orchestrator):\n#   N        — number of rounds for `make loop` (default 10).\n#   K        — tournament size, slots per round (default 1 = sequential).\n#   AGENT    — codex (default) or claude. Honors a pre-existing\n#              AGENT_PROVIDER env var if AGENT isn't set on the make\n#              command line.\n#   BASE     — when forking a new TARGET, copy from cores/<BASE>/.\n#              Default: baseline (orchestrator-side default).\n#   COREMARK — target CoreMark iterations/sec (e.g. '370').\n#   LUT      — target LUT count (e.g. '3000').\n#   WORKTREE — default ON. `make loop` first creates a dedicated git worktree\n#              at .worktrees/<TARGET>/ on branch core-<TARGET> and re-execs\n#              itself there. Lets two `make loop` invocations for different\n#              TARGETs run in parallel without git index/merge collisions.\n#              To opt out (run directly on the current branch + cwd) pass\n#              an explicit empty value: `make loop TARGET=v1 WORKTREE=`.\nN        ?= 10\nK        ?= 1\nAGENT    ?= $(or $(AGENT_PROVIDER),codex)\nBASE     ?=\nCOREMARK ?=\nLUT      ?=\nWORKTREE ?= 1\n\n# Compose optional CLI flags for the orchestrator. Empty vars produce\n# empty strings so the orchestrator falls back to its defaults.\nORCH_FLAGS  = --iterations $(N) --tournament-size $(K)\nifneq ($(strip $(BASE)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --base $(BASE)\nendif\nifneq ($(strip $(COREMARK)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --coremark-target $(COREMARK)\nendif\nifneq ($(strip $(LUT)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --lut-target $(LUT)\nendif\n\n# Multi-core: TARGET selects the core under cores/<TARGET>\n…[7904 of 10976 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:985d56ef2bfba5b9]…\n_runner():\n976:    # when the runner compiles from its separate build directory.\n977:    runner = get_runner(os.environ.get(\"SIM\", \"verilator\"))\n979:    runner.build(\n992:    runner.test(\nrg: tools/eval/timing.py: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ntools/eval/fpga.py:93:async def run_seed(seed: int, worktree: str, outdir: str, env: dict | None = None) -> dict:\ntools/eval/fpga.py:203:def run_coremark_ipc(worktree: str, sim_bin: str | None = None, env: dict | None = None) -> dict:\ntools/eval/fpga.py:330:def run_fpga_eval(worktree: str, target: str | None = None) -> dict:\ntools/eval/gowin.py:199:def main(argv=None) -> int:\ntools/eval/gowin.py:202:    import argparse, json\ntools/eval/gowin.py:204:    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\ntools/eval/gowin.py:205:    ap.add_argument(\"target\")\ntools/eval/gowin.py:206:    ap.add_argument(\"--worktree\", default=\".\")\ntools/eval/gowin.py:207:    ap.add_argument(\"--paths\", type=int, default=5)\ntools/eval/gowin.py:208:    ap.add_argument(\"--all-options\", action=\"store_true\",\n", "exit_code": 2, "status": "failed"}}
