{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_74", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nimport yaml\nimport json\nimport jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r5s2.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261003-003-r5s2\ntitle: \\\"Reuse the predictor's direct target through an acceptance-latched target field\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion already predicts direct JAL and uses sixteen two-bit agree\n  counters for conditional branches, achieving 4,203,513 bracketed CoreMark\n  cycles at 47.574 MHz and fitness 113.18. Prior 128-entry predictors lost\n  timing margin, and the recorded architectural trace estimates only\n  55,124 remaining conditional-direction misses: perfect direction alone\n  would save about 1.3% of current cycles. Predictor hardware cost is the\n  more promising angle than increasing direction-table complexity.\n\n  Fetch already computes the exact full-width PC-relative destination for\n  every direct branch/JAL, independently of its predicted direction. EX\n  nevertheless reconstructs the same destination with another PC-plus-\n  immediate adder. Reusing that instruction-derived destination removes\n  redundant target arithmetic from the recovery network while retaining\n  the champion's prediction behavior. Proposal-stage probes found this\n  variant better than smaller tables, static prediction, one-bit training,\n  or single-bit recovery squash, although none cleared the acceptance bar.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a direct_target field to the combinational IF/ID bundle and its own\n  acceptance-latched field in ID/EX. Drive it from the existing IF\n  direct_target = pc + direct_imm computation on raw imem_data. Capture\n  this value alongside the instruction and predicted_taken at the same\n  edge; hold it on every ID/EX stall and clear it with reset/flush.\n  Preserve the existing immediate field and every current capture enable.\n  This is one predictor-datapath change: reuse the front end's exact\n  instruction-derived destination for direct-transfer resolution.\n\n  Carry the raw computed destination even for a predicted-not-taken\n  conditional branch and even when target alignment suppresses prediction.\n  It must not be next_pc, the selected prediction, or an aligned/truncated\n  version of the destination. EX needs the original low target bits to\n  preserve misalignment traps, and a missed taken branch needs its real\n  target rather than PC+4. Use all 32 target bits, including wraparound.\n\n  In EX replace branch_target = in.pc + in.imm with the captured\n  in.direct_target. For JAL select the same captured direct_target. For\n  JALR retain the forwarded rs1 + original immediate computation and bit-0\n  clearing. Preserve all existing branch comparisons, legality checks,\n  misalignment detection, actual_taken, direction-XOR recovery, PC+4 link\n  writes and resolved architectural pc_next. Direction prediction remains\n  speculative; this target is exact for its accepted direct instruction\n  because it was calculated from that instruction's PC and immediate.\n  No BTB, target alias, target prediction, or target-match comparator is\n  introduced. Non-control instructions ignore the new field.\n\n  Keep the sixteen PC[5:2]-indexed agreement counters, displacement-sign\n  bias, saturation, reset value, local training and read-before-write\n  behavior unchanged. Keep JALR sequential prediction, one-shot training\n  on valid non-faulting EX advance, immediate recovery priority over imem\n  stalls, and all current squash and memory/divider hold rules. Do not\n  combine this proposal with counter resizing or recovery retiming. Keep\n  nret=1, decoded immediates, real/ALTOPS arithmetic, decoder defaults,\n  forwarding and all retirement invariants unchanged.\n\n  An exact temporary prototype with a separate ID/EX direct_target field\n  measured Gowin placement frequencies 46.472, 48.336 and 48.336 MHz,\n  for median 48.336 MHz. Logic fell from 3,181 to 3,070; registers rose\n  from 675 to 706. The existing 23-test pipeline suite passed. The\n  unchanged CoreMark IPC evaluator passed canonical CRC/UART and marker\n  validation and measured exactly 4,203,513 cycles for ten iterations\n  with both buses stalled. This projects fitness 114.9895, approximately\n  1.60% above 113.18. These are proposal-stage measurements, not a recorded\n  tournament acceptance. The exact separate-field variant has not yet\n  completed the full formal and full-trace cosim gates.\n\n  Expect about 2% fitness improvement with low confidence in acceptance.\n  The measured probe does NOT exceed the required 4.6% margin: fitness\n  must exceed 118.38628, requiring about 49.765 MHz at unchanged cycles.\n  The unchanged multiplier/forwarding path remains clock-limiting, so\n  removing target logic may not provide enough timing headroom. Prefer\n  this narrowly scoped, measured predictor improvement to claiming an\n  unsupported gain above the threshold; the implementation phase must\n  rerun the actual median and all unchanged correctness gates.\n\n  Extend the existing prediction scoreboard to check that accepted\n  direct_target metadata matches independent full-width PC-plus-immediate\n  calculation and stays paired with its instruction under stalls. Cover\n  correctly predicted and mispredicted branches, predicted-not-taken\n  branches that resolve taken, direct JAL links, JALR fallback, targets\n  equal to PC+4, negative displacements, address carry/wrap boundaries,\n  misaligned direct targets, reserved encodings, reset, load-use replay,\n  imem backpressure on recovery, dmem release and divider holds. Retain\n  wrong-path store/divide/illegal-instruction checks and exact RVFI PC,\n  order, operand, trap and progress assertions. Preserve every formal,\n  cosim, canonical CRC/UART, memory-bound and marker-only timing gate.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Add a 32-bit direct_target field to if_id_t and id_ex_t. Keep the\n      original immediate and all resolved downstream RVFI fields intact.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Expose the existing raw instruction-derived direct_target in the\n      IF/ID bundle, independently of direction and alignment suppression.\n      Preserve all predictor, PC, validity and flush logic.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture direct_target with the accepted instruction. Hold and clear\n      it with the same existing stall, reset and flush rules as its bundle.\n      Keep original immediate capture and decoder controls unchanged.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Use captured direct_target for conditional-branch and direct-JAL\n      destinations, removing their duplicate PC-plus-immediate arithmetic.\n      Preserve forwarded JALR target generation, traps, link writes,\n      direction recovery, predictor training and architectural pc_next.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Extend target and acceptance scoreboarding across prediction errors,\n      stalls, address carries/wrap, alignment faults and consecutive\n      transfers. Preserve existing architectural assertions and verify\n      unchanged recovery bubble count and no wrong-path side effects.\n  - file: test/test_if_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Check the unselected direct_target independently of predicted_taken,\n      including predicted-not-taken branches and misaligned destinations.\n      Adapt packed-bundle extraction if needed while preserving all counter,\n      PC priority, acceptance and saturation checks.\n''')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261003-003-r5s2' and d['category']=='predictor'\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nb=Path('cores/bench/generated/r5s2-proposal-original')\nfor f in b.iterdir():\n shutil.copyfile(f,Path('cores/bench/test' if f.suffix=='.py' else 'cores/bench/rtl')/f.name)\nprint('Final hypothesis written and schema-valid. Temporary RTL/test changes restored.')\nprint('Hypothesis bytes:',p.stat().st_size)\nPY\ngit status --short\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
