{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor':\n  print('\\\\n', d['id'], d['title'], 'fitness',d.get('fitness'),'cycles',d.get('cycles'),'fmax',d.get('fmax_mhz'))\n  if d['id'].endswith('r5s2') or d['id'].endswith('r4s2'):\n   h=d['hypothesis']; print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\n hyp-20261003-003-r1s2 Instruction-aware bimodal prediction for the fused fetch/decode stage fitness 12.97 cycles 4202272 fmax 5.452\n\n hyp-20261003-003-r2s2 Apply instruction-aware bimodal prediction to the multicycle-divider champion fitness 74.95 cycles 4202272 fmax 31.494\n\n hyp-20261003-003-r3s2 Timing-lean bimodal prediction with direction-only recovery fitness 96.91 cycles 4202272 fmax 40.725\n\n hyp-20261003-003-r4s2 Sixteen-entry agree prediction with instruction-derived branch bias fitness 113.18 cycles 4203513 fmax 47.574\nAdd a compact instruction-biased agree predictor to the existing fused\nfetch/decode stage. This is one predictor architecture change: replace\nabsolute taken/not-taken learning with learning agreement with a branch's\nown static direction bias, allowing just sixteen two-bit counters indexed\nby fetch PC[5:2]. Use backward-taken/forward-not-taken bias, where bias is\nthe raw branch instruction's bit 31. Counter MSB one predicts agreement\nwith that bias; MSB zero predicts its inverse. Equivalently, conditional\npredicted_taken = bias XNOR counter[1]. Reset every counter to 2'b10,\nweakly agree. Train toward agreement when actual_taken equals bias and\ntoward disagreement otherwise, with conventional unsigned saturation.\nOppositely biased branches sharing a counter can reinforce each other\ninstead of fighting over an absolute direction. No benchmark PC constants\nor instruction-address-specific initialization are permitted.\n\nPredict only legal BRANCH encodings using this table. Predict direct JAL\ntaken unconditionally, obtaining both B and J targets from the current\nraw instruction's sign-extended immediate plus the full 32-bit fetch PC.\nRequire word-aligned direct targets before selecting them. JALR and all\nother instructions predict PC+4; reserved branch encodings and misaligned\ndirect targets retain sequential prediction and existing trap handling.\nNo target cache, return stack, global history, added stage, or arithmetic\nchange is part of this proposal.\n\nImplement sixteen constant-index counter \n…[6926 of 9998 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:43765a9f466afb94]…\nn above the threshold; the implementation phase must\nrerun the actual median and all unchanged correctness gates.\n\nExtend the existing prediction scoreboard to check that accepted\ndirect_target metadata matches independent full-width PC-plus-immediate\ncalculation and stays paired with its instruction under stalls. Cover\ncorrectly predicted and mispredicted branches, predicted-not-taken\nbranches that resolve taken, direct JAL links, JALR fallback, targets\nequal to PC+4, negative displacements, address carry/wrap boundaries,\nmisaligned direct targets, reserved encodings, reset, load-use replay,\nimem backpressure on recovery, dmem release and divider holds. Retain\nwrong-path store/divide/illegal-instruction checks and exact RVFI PC,\norder, operand, trap and progress assertions. Preserve every formal,\ncosim, canonical CRC/UART, memory-bound and marker-only timing gate.\n\n\n hyp-20261003-003-r6s2 Move predictor squash to a registered EX kill bit and keep fetch data unmasked fitness 123.92 cycles 4203513 fmax 52.089\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
