{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_53", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r7s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261003-003-r7s2',\n 'title':'Preselect the opposite prediction offset for immediate branch recovery',\n 'category':'predictor',\n 'motivation':'''The champion's sixteen-entry agree predictor already removes most control-flow bubbles. Prior tracing estimated only 55,124 conditional misses and 13,735 JALRs in 4,203,513 bracketed cycles, leaving little accuracy headroom. Direct-target reuse and delayed EX annulment previously failed the acceptance margin. Current EX recovery routes resolved_pc_next to IF: a late forwarded-operand branch comparison selects a full-width address before PC repair. On a direction mismatch, the saved prediction already identifies the required recovery destination. Preparing that address independently is a narrowly scoped predictor timing hypothesis.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Separate the speculative recovery-address datapath from the architectural resolved-next-PC datapath. Preserve the current sixteen-entry agree predictor, direct-JAL prediction, direction-XOR recovery detection, training, immediate PC repair, and single-bubble miss penalty. Select the recovery displacement before addition using the prediction already saved in ID/EX.\n\nIn ex_stage, compute recovery_offset = in.predicted_taken ? 32'd4 : in.imm and recovery_direct = in.pc + recovery_offset. Drive redirect_target = (in.ctrl.is_jalr && \"'!in.predicted_taken) ? {jalr_sum[31:1], 1'\"'b0} : recovery_direct, reusing the existing full-width forwarded rs1+imm jalr_sum. Keep redirect = in.valid && ex_advance && (actual_taken \"'^ in.predicted_taken) unchanged. Do not add a prediction-inversion field, counter-update register, target register or pipeline stage.\n\nCorrectness follows from the existing mismatch condition: whenever redirect is asserted, actual_taken is the inverse of in.predicted_taken. A false taken prediction therefore repairs to PC+4, and a missed taken direct transfer repairs to PC+imm. An unpredicted legal JALR uses its forwarded target with bit zero cleared. The !in.predicted_taken qualification on the JALR selection also preserves sequential recovery if a predicted-taken instruction were to resolve to a fault. Use the prediction captured with this exact accepted instruction, never the live table lookup.\n\nThe prepared recovery address need equal resolved_pc_next only while redirect is asserted. Keep the existing actual-outcome calculation of resolved_pc_next for EX/MEM pc_next and RVFI pc_wdata; do not substitute the speculative recovery address there. Preserve original PC+4 link writes, branch comparisons, full 32-bit modular arithmetic, legality checks, JALR masking, target-misalignment suppression, and sequential architectural next PC on traps. Preserve the independent effective-address register and all real/ALTOPS arithmetic.\n\nLeave ex_advance'\"'s reset, dmem-stall and execute-wait qualifications intact. IF retains reset then accepted redirect then ordinary accepted prediction as PC-update priorities. Recovery still overrides imem backpressure on dmem release and squashes the younger slot before any side effect. Prediction metadata holds with its instruction through memory freezes, load-use replay and division. No accuracy improvement or reduced miss penalty is claimed. Keep nret=1, retirement order, all bus handshakes and every existing progress bound and correctness gate.\n\nThe intended mechanism removes the actual branch outcome from the wide recovery-address mux and moves the displacement choice ahead of a PC adder. It leaves only the one-bit redirect enable dependent on late resolution. This does not remove the champion's divider/multiplier timing limit, and actual Gowin results do not currently support a net gain.\n\nAn exact temporary prototype passed the existing IF and pipeline cocotb suites without changing their assertions, plus selftest RVFI cosimulation with ready buses and with both buses stalled. The unchanged CoreMark IPC evaluator passed canonical CRC/UART, bounds and marker validation at exactly 4,203,513 bracketed cycles for ten iterations. Gowin placement options measured 50.671, 53.799 and 53.799 MHz, giving median 53.799 MHz; option-zero usage was 3,170 logic cells, 701 registers, eight LUT RAMs, six BSRAMs and six DSPs. These are proposal-stage measurements, not tournament acceptance.\n\nThat measured product is fitness 127.9858, approximately 4.34 percent BELOW the 133.79 champion. The integer expected impact is consequently -4 percent, with low confidence in an eventual improvement. This hypothesis does NOT clear the required 4.6 percent acceptance margin. At unchanged cycles it would need median Fmax strictly above approximately 58.826 MHz. Retain this explicit negative result rather than claiming that shorter logical feedback implies a faster FPGA. Implementation must rerun all unchanged gates and the scored median; do not relax checks or accept below the required fitness product.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':-4,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Add recovery_offset and recovery_direct combinational wires. Select constant four versus in.imm from the saved predicted_taken bit before the PC adder; select the existing aligned JALR sum only for is_jalr && \"'!predicted_taken. Drive redirect_target from this prepared address. Preserve direction-XOR detection, immediate repair, actual-outcome resolved_pc_next/RVFI, traps, training, links, arithmetic and every advance/hold condition. Document conditional equivalence of recovery and architectural next PC whenever redirect is asserted.'\"'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Extend the independent recovery scoreboard to check the prepared address for each accepted mismatch while retaining all architectural assertions. Cover false-taken and missed-taken branches, every branch condition, direct JAL, JALR with forwarded and load-produced bases, PC+4-equivalent targets, negative offsets and full-width carry/wrap, misaligned transfers, illegal encodings, adjacent transfers, dmem holds/release, imem-stalled recovery, division and reset. Check actual-outcome RVFI pc_wdata on both correct and incorrect predictions, unchanged miss/progress bounds, and absence of wrong-path store/divider activity. The existing suite passed the temporary prototype unchanged; additions must strengthen coverage, not weaken expectations.'''}]}\nclass BlockDumper(yaml.SafeDumper):\n pass\ndef represent_str(dumper,data):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',data,style='|' if '\\\\n' in data or len(data)>150 else None)\nBlockDumper.add_representer(str,represent_str)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=BlockDumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final measured hypothesis written and schema-valid.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
