assed the existing IF and pipeline cocotb suites without changing their assertions, plus selftest RVFI cosimulation with ready buses and with both buses stalled. The unchanged CoreMark IPC evaluator passed canonical CRC/UART, bounds and marker validation at exactly 4,203,513 bracketed cycles for ten iterations. Gowin placement options measured 50.671, 53.799 and 53.799 MHz, giving median 53.799 MHz; option-zero usage was 3,170 logic cells, 701 registers, eight LUT RAMs, six BSRAMs and six DSPs. These are proposal-stage measurements, not tournament acceptance.\n\nThat measured product is fitness 127.9858, approximately 4.34 percent BELOW the 133.79 champion. The integer expected impact is consequently -4 percent, with low confidence in an eventual improvement. This hypothesis does NOT clear the required 4.6 percent acceptance margin. At unchanged cycles it would need median Fmax strictly above approximately 58.826 MHz. Retain this explicit negative result rather than claiming that shorter logical feedback implies a faster FPGA. Implementation must rerun all unchanged gates and the scored median; do not relax checks or accept below the required fitness product.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':-4,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Add recovery_offset and recovery_direct combinational wires. Select constant four versus in.imm from the saved predicted_taken bit before the PC adder; select the existing aligned JALR sum only for is_jalr && \"'!predicted_taken. Drive redirect_target from this prepared address. Preserve direction-XOR detection, immediate repair, actual-outcome resolved_pc_next/RVFI, traps, training, links, arithmetic and every advance/hold condition. Document conditional equivalence of recovery and architectural next PC whenever redirect is asserted.'\"'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Extend the independent recovery scoreboard to check the prepared address for each accepted mismatch while retaining all architectural assertions. Cover false-taken and missed-taken branches, every branch condition, direct JAL, JALR with forwarded and load-produced bases, PC+4-equivalent targets, negative offsets and full-width carry/wrap, misaligned transfers, illegal encodings, adjacent transfers, dmem holds/release, imem-stalled recovery, division and reset. Check actual-outcome RVFI pc_wdata on both correct and incorrect predictions, unchanged miss/progress bounds, and absence of wrong-path store/divider activity. The existing suite passed the temporary prototype unchanged; additions must strengthen coverage, not weaken expectations.'''}]}\nclass BlockDumper(yaml.SafeDumper):\n pass\ndef represent_str(dumper,data):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',data,style='|' if '\\\\n' in data or len(data)>150 else None)\nBlockDumper.add_representer(str,represent_str)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=BlockDumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final measured hypothesis written and schema-valid.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Final measured hypothesis written and schema-valid.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
