dix-4 digits, improving fitness without increasing the nine-clock DIV/REM latency.\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r4s0 (regression, +8.24%): Removing the IF instruction-to-NOP mux shortened the redirect-to-hazard control path and raised median Gowin Fmax to 50.514 MHz at unchanged CoreMark cyc\n…[154149 of 157221 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b32a215f2f07596b]…\n\"cycles\": 4203513, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3170, \"ff\": 701, \"seeds\": [50.671, 53.799, 53.799], \"perturbations\": [[0, 50.671, 20], [1, 53.799, 24], [2, 53.799, 24]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_ER_s195\", \"slack_ns\": -14.735, \"arrival_ns\": 25.03, \"logic_cells\": 46, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_rf\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 20, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T19:11:51.719996Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 7, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r7s2 (regression, -4.34%): Preselecting `predicted_taken ? 4 : imm` before the EX recovery adder removes late branch resolution from target selection without addressing divider/multiplier timing limits or reducing CoreMark cycles, so shorter logical recovery feedback does not guarantee faster Gowin timing (median Fmax fell from 56.239 to 53.799 MHz).\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
