{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r8s2.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nh=d['hypothesis']\na=h.index('Read the counter MSBs')\nb=h.index('\\\\n\\\\nThe PC and agreement',a)\nh=h[:a]+'''Compute one four-bit next_predict_index: redirect ? redirect_target[5:2] : predicted_taken ? direct_target[5:2] : pc[5:2] + 4'd1. Read agree_msb[next_predict_index] and capture it into predict_agree_q only when the PC register updates. Reset sets the bit to one; otherwise redirect || \"'!stall enables capture; otherwise hold. Redirect takes priority in both the index mux and PC update, including during stalls. Select the narrow index before one shared asynchronous MSB lookup; do not replicate three candidate lookup trees. The table remains sixteen local counter cells with its existing update logic and no new memory primitive.'\"'''+h[b:]\nh=h.replace('at the cost of one register and three narrow lookups.', 'at the cost of one register, a four-bit index mux and a four-bit sequential-index increment.')\na=h.index('An initial common-index')\nh=h[:a]+'''A temporary prototype of this exact common-index lookahead design measured Gowin placement frequencies 49.152, 53.311 and 53.311 MHz, with median 53.311 MHz. Option-zero usage was 3,127 logic cells, 702 registers, eight LUT RAMs, six BSRAMs and six DSPs. Selftest cosimulation and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation passed; CoreMark measured 4,203,504 bracketed cycles for ten iterations. A same-session unchanged-reference build reproduced the champion's 56.239 MHz median. These are proposal-stage measurements, not tournament acceptance.\n\nThat measured product is approximately 126.83 fitness, about 5.2 percent BELOW the 133.79 champion. Expected impact is therefore -5 percent with low confidence in improvement. This candidate does NOT clear the 4.6 percent acceptance margin. Acceptance requires a measured product strictly above 139.94434, about 58.826 MHz at this cycle count. The unchanged divider/multiplier and recovery paths still limit timing; removal of an asynchronous lookup from one path is not evidence of a whole-core speedup. Implement and remeasure normally without relaxing any correctness or timing gates. Temporary RTL and test probes are restored after validation, leaving this YAML as the deliverable.'''\nd['hypothesis']=h\nd['changes'][0]['description']='''Add a reset-to-one predict_agree_q register whose update enable matches PC: redirect || \"'!stall. Compute the next four-bit counter index using redirect, predicted direct target, or sequential PC+4 priority and capture the current table MSB at that index. Use this snapshot in conditional prediction instead of a live current-PC table lookup. Keep all sixteen counter cells, immediate EX training, branch legality/alignment, target arithmetic, output masking, PC repair and captured prediction metadata otherwise unchanged. No training bypass or snapshot refresh during a PC hold.'\"'''\nclass D(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef multiline(dumper,value):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',value,style='|' if '\\\\n' in value or len(value)>120 else None)\nD.add_representer(str,multiline)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=D,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final candidate schema valid')\nprint('Fitness:',53.311e6*10/4203504,'delta pct:',(53.311e6*10/4203504/133.79-1)*100)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
