{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_89", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r9s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261003-003-r9s2\ntitle: \"Compile the saved prediction into a direct branch-miss predicate\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The sixteen-entry agreement predictor already leaves little cycle headroom:\n  earlier tracing estimated 55,124 conditional misses and 13,735 JALRs in\n  4,203,513 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Recent worst paths repeatedly cross EX\n  recovery, IF masking and register-file controls. Larger tables or a return\n  predictor cannot plausibly clear the 4.6 percent margin from cycle savings\n  alone. Target preselection in r7s2 and a registered predictor lookup in r8s2\n  both regressed. Attack the late recovery-enable calculation itself while\n  retaining the current predictor, acceptance rules and one-bubble miss penalty.\nhypothesis: |\n  Compile each accepted branch's prediction into a decode-time recovery\n  descriptor, so EX directly evaluates whether the prediction was wrong instead\n  of resolving direction, qualifying actual_taken, then XORing predicted_taken.\n  Keep the sixteen local agreement counters, sign bias, immediate training,\n  raw-instruction prediction, direct-JAL prediction and current pipeline depth.\n  This is one predictor-recovery timing change, not an accuracy experiment.\n\n  Add to id_ex_t a three-bit miss_branch_op and a branch_recovery_enable bit.\n  In ID, miss_branch_op = decoded branch_op XOR {2'b00, in.predicted_taken}.\n  The low funct3 bit complements each legal relation: BEQ/BNE, BLT/BGE and\n  BLTU/BGEU. Compute branch_recovery_enable from legal conditional-branch\n  decode and word alignment of the direct target. Determine alignment with\n  the exact two-bit sum of in.pc[1:0] and imm[1:0], without a new full-width\n  adder. Capture both fields with the same instruction and exact prediction\n  used to advance fetch; hold on stalls and clear on reset or flush.\n\n  EX evaluates one set of forwarded equality, signed-less-than and\n  unsigned-less-than predicates. Use the captured miss_branch_op to select\n  the appropriate predicate or its complement directly as branch_miss.\n \n…[4865 of 7937 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9c1549e49fc1f463]…\n      unpredicted JALR on EX advance. Keep the original redirect_target,\n      actual-outcome pc_next, traps, predictor training, link results,\n      divider behavior and effective-address capture unchanged.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Keep all existing assertions and prediction scoreboards; adjust packed\n      ID/EX field offsets solely for the four added descriptor bits. Add a directed\n      cross-product of all six branch relations, both saved predictions,\n      taken/not-taken outcomes, signed extremes and equality boundaries.\n      Exercise aliases that change the live table after acceptance, load/WB\n      forwarding, holds, imem-stalled recovery, aligned/misaligned direct\n      targets and JALR, reserved encodings, wrong-path memory/divide activity,\n      reset and full-width wraparound. Assert equivalence to resolved-next-PC\n      recovery for each accepted instruction, exact once-only training and\n      unchanged one-bubble misses and ten-clock redirected-divide progress.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
