{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_51", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r14s0.yaml')\nd=dict(id='hyp-20261004-001-r14s0',title='Collapse two serial radix-4 divider digits into one parallel radix-16 step',category='micro_opt',motivation='''The champion achieves 191.41 fitness at 81.140 MHz and 4,239,051 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its branch recovery, divider completion and two-digit divider recurrence are close competing limits. Local control-cone probes moved the worst paths into the unchanged recurrence without improving scored Fmax. Prior r3s0 and a fresh split-subtractor probe show that replacing native carry chains with routed block-prefix or carry-select networks is counterproductive. Instead, remove the serial dependence between the two radix-4 digits in each ordinary divider round while retaining native subtractors and the complete sequential protocol.''',hypothesis='''Replace only the real-arithmetic nonfinal divider recurrence in alu.sv with one parallel radix-16 digit. Each existing ordinary round consumes four dividend bits, exactly as the current pair of serial radix-4 digits does. Keep operand capture at edge zero, seven four-bit rounds at edges one through seven, and the existing single radix-4 prefix-transfer computation at edge eight. Keep the final radix-4 digit and signed candidate selection in m_finish.sv unchanged. This is a combinational recurrence implementation change, with no new stage, instruction latency or scheduling policy.\n\nCapture eight unsigned 36-bit odd divisor multiples D,3D,5D,7D,9D,11D,13D,15D from the normalized divisor at the existing request edge. All even multiples are constant left shifts of the appropriate captured odd multiple. Widen to 36 bits before shifting or adding: 15*(2\"'^32-1) requires all 36 bits. Compute 3D,5D,9D by one shifted addition, 7D and 15D by shifted subtraction, and 11D=D+2D+8D and 13D=D+4D+8D with bitwise carry-save reduction followed by one native carry-propagate addition. Do not cascade two full adders to form those latter multiples. Retain the existing captured 34-bit D and 3D for the final radix-4 token, allowing synthesis to share duplicate register bits. Reset the new multiple registers consistently with existing divider state and update them only on a request accepted in DIV_IDLE.\n\nIn each nonfinal round form unsigned T={remainder_q,quotient_q[31:28]}, width 36. Compute fifteen independent 37-bit zero-extended differences T-kD for k=1..15. Difference bit 36 is the borrow. Use the ordered threshold results to select the largest non-borrowing k: select[0]=borrow[1], select[15]=!borrow[15], and select[k]=!borrow[k] && borrow[k+1] otherwise. For positive D, the remainder invariant R<D gives T<16D, so the selected remainder satisfies 0<=T-kD<D and fits 32 bits. For D=0 every comparison succeeds, select[15] is the only active bit, and the consumed dividend prefix is retained as remainder. Never truncate the trial or divisor multiples before the borrow decisions.\n\nPrepare sixteen masked 36-bit candidates {remainder_candidate[31:0],4-bit k}, with k=0 using T[31:0], and combine them in an explicit balanced binary OR tree. Set remainder_next to the upper 32 selected bits and quotient_next={quotient_q[27:0],selected_digit}. The original radix-4 logic is still required for the single edge-eight prefix digit; reduce its elaborated loop from two digits to one and keep token selection, DIV_DONE capture-once behavior and consume timing identical. The second radix-4 digit is replaced, not retained as dead parallel arithmetic.\n\nPreserve magnitude capture, signed quotient and dividend-signed remainder semantics, zero divisors, INT_MIN/-1, reset cancellation, held operands, final-prefix availability independent of consume, blocked completion, back-to-back division and independence of younger M operations. Keep the original RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS arithmetic and exactly the same schedule in both configurations. Multiplication, integer ALU operations, decoder legality, forwarding, pipeline controls, memory requests, prediction and nret=1 remain unchanged. Modify no evaluator or formal contract.\n\nValidate every four-bit round against an independent integer divmod model, all sixteen selected digits, thresholds around kD, high unsigned divisors, all signed combinations, zero divisors and overflow. Existing tests already check every registered four-bit prefix and must retain their exact latency, hold and reset assertions. Run ALU real/ALTOPS tests, pipeline tests, unchanged formal/liveness and stalled CoreMark cosimulation with canonical CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation. Prove local equivalence of the radix-16 recurrence to two radix-4 steps under the reachable remainder invariant; normal ALTOPS formal cannot establish real divider arithmetic.\n\nThe intended gain is shorter arithmetic depth at unchanged CoreMark cycles. The area and routing cost of fifteen trial subtractors and additional divisor-multiple registers is substantial; branch recovery, M completion or operand-capture-to-multiple paths may become limiting. Confidence is low until vendor timing is measured. Acceptance requires measured fitness strictly above 200.21486, approximately 84.872 MHz at unchanged cycles. Proposal-stage measurements will be recorded here before finalization; no improvement is yet claimed.'\"''',expected_impact=dict(fitness_delta_pct=8,confidence='low'),changes=[dict(file='rtl/alu.sv',description='Capture full-width odd divisor multiples and replace two serial radix-4 digits per nonfinal round with fifteen parallel native trial subtractors, ordered borrow selection and a balanced sixteen-candidate reduction. Retain one radix-4 digit for prefix transfer, the existing token format, all real/ALTOPS schedules, state transitions and every other ALU operation.'),dict(file='test/test_alu.py',description='Extend the existing integer-model prefix checks with all sixteen radix-16 digits, kD threshold neighbors, full-width odd multiples, unsigned high divisors and signed exceptional cases. Preserve all current exact latency, early-consume, held-token, back-to-back request and reset assertions; continue testing composed X-to-M-to-W real and ALTOPS arithmetic.')])\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=80))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Updated and schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_51", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r14s0.yaml')\nd=dict(id='hyp-20261004-001-r14s0',title='Collapse two serial radix-4 divider digits into one parallel radix-16 step',category='micro_opt',motivation='''The champion achieves 191.41 fitness at 81.140 MHz and 4,239,051 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its branch recovery, divider completion and two-digit divider recurrence are close competing limits. Local control-cone probes moved the worst paths into the unchanged recurrence without improving scored Fmax. Prior r3s0 and a fresh split-subtractor probe show that replacing native carry chains with routed block-prefix or carry-select networks is counterproductive. Instead, remove the serial dependence between the two radix-4 digits in each ordinary divider round while retaining native subtractors and the complete sequential protocol.''',hypothesis='''Replace only the real-arithmetic nonfinal divider recurrence in alu.sv with one parallel radix-16 digit. Each existing ordinary round consumes four dividend bits, exactly as the current pair of serial radix-4 digits does. Keep operand capture at edge zero, seven four-bit rounds at edges one through seven, and the existing single radix-4 prefix-transfer computation at edge eight. Keep the final radix-4 digit and signed candidate selection in m_finish.sv unchanged. This is a combinational recurrence implementation change, with no new stage, instruction latency or scheduling policy.\n\nCapture eight unsigned 36-bit odd divisor multiples D,3D,5D,7D,9D,11D,13D,15D from the normalized divisor at the existing request edge. All even multiples are constant left shifts of the appropriate captured odd multiple. Widen to 36 bits before shifting or adding: 15*(2\"'^32-1) requires all 36 bits. Compute 3D,5D,9D by one shifted addition, 7D and 15D by shifted subtraction, and 11D=D+2D+8D and 13D=D+4D+8D with bitwise carry-save reduction followed by one native carry-propagate addition. Do not cascade two full adders to form those latter multiples. Retain the existing captured 34-bit D and 3D for the final radix-4 token, allowing synthesis to share duplicate register bits. Reset the new multiple registers consistently with existing divider state and update them only on a request accepted in DIV_IDLE.\n\nIn each nonfinal round form unsigned T={remainder_q,quotient_q[31:28]}, width 36. Compute fifteen independent 37-bit zero-extended differences T-kD for k=1..15. Difference bit 36 is the borrow. Use the ordered threshold results to select the largest non-borrowing k: select[0]=borrow[1], select[15]=!borrow[15], and select[k]=!borrow[k] && borrow[k+1] otherwise. For positive D, the remainder invariant R<D gives T<16D, so the selected remainder satisfies 0<=T-kD<D and fits 32 bits. For D=0 every comparison succeeds, select[15] is the only active bit, and the consumed dividend prefix is retained as remainder. Never truncate the trial or divisor multiples before the borrow decisions.\n\nPrepare sixteen masked 36-bit candidates {remainder_candidate[31:0],4-bit k}, with k=0 using T[31:0], and combine them in an explicit balanced binary OR tree. Set remainder_next to the upper 32 selected bits and quotient_next={quotient_q[27:0],selected_digit}. The original radix-4 logic is still required for the single edge-eight prefix digit; reduce its elaborated loop from two digits to one and keep token selection, DIV_DONE capture-once behavior and consume timing identical. The second radix-4 digit is replaced, not retained as dead parallel arithmetic.\n\nPreserve magnitude capture, signed quotient and dividend-signed remainder semantics, zero divisors, INT_MIN/-1, reset cancellation, held operands, final-prefix availability independent of consume, blocked completion, back-to-back division and independence of younger M operations. Keep the original RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS arithmetic and exactly the same schedule in both configurations. Multiplication, integer ALU operations, decoder legality, forwarding, pipeline controls, memory requests, prediction and nret=1 remain unchanged. Modify no evaluator or formal contract.\n\nValidate every four-bit round against an independent integer divmod model, all sixteen selected digits, thresholds around kD, high unsigned divisors, all signed combinations, zero divisors and overflow. Existing tests already check every registered four-bit prefix and must retain their exact latency, hold and reset assertions. Run ALU real/ALTOPS tests, pipeline tests, unchanged formal/liveness and stalled CoreMark cosimulation with canonical CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation. Prove local equivalence of the radix-16 recurrence to two radix-4 steps under the reachable remainder invariant; normal ALTOPS formal cannot establish real divider arithmetic.\n\nThe intended gain is shorter arithmetic depth at unchanged CoreMark cycles. The area and routing cost of fifteen trial subtractors and additional divisor-multiple registers is substantial; branch recovery, M completion or operand-capture-to-multiple paths may become limiting. Confidence is low until vendor timing is measured. Acceptance requires measured fitness strictly above 200.21486, approximately 84.872 MHz at unchanged cycles. Proposal-stage measurements will be recorded here before finalization; no improvement is yet claimed.'\"''',expected_impact=dict(fitness_delta_pct=8,confidence='low'),changes=[dict(file='rtl/alu.sv',description='Capture full-width odd divisor multiples and replace two serial radix-4 digits per nonfinal round with fifteen parallel native trial subtractors, ordered borrow selection and a balanced sixteen-candidate reduction. Retain one radix-4 digit for prefix transfer, the existing token format, all real/ALTOPS schedules, state transitions and every other ALU operation.'),dict(file='test/test_alu.py',description='Extend the existing integer-model prefix checks with all sixteen radix-16 digits, kD threshold neighbors, full-width odd multiples, unsigned high divisors and signed exceptional cases. Preserve all current exact latency, early-consume, held-token, back-to-back request and reset assertions; continue testing composed X-to-M-to-W real and ALTOPS arithmetic.')])\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=80))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Updated and schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
