{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_63", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r14s0.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Finish unsigned division in X with parallel radix-16 trials at unchanged latency'\nh=d['hypothesis']\na=h.index('Replace only');z=h.index('\\\\n\\\\nCapture eight')\nh='''Replace the real-arithmetic divider recurrence with one parallel radix-16 digit per round. Keep magnitude capture at edge zero and perform eight four-bit rounds at edges one through eight. The last round presents COMPLETE unsigned quotient and remainder to EX/MEM at the same edge eight that currently transfers a thirty-bit prefix. M then only selects quotient versus remainder and performs the existing captured sign correction before W. Nine-clock X occupancy, M completion, dependent-instruction stalls and retirement timing remain identical. This single local divider optimization uses radix-16 arithmetic to remove both serial radix-4 recurrence and M's final trial subtraction; it adds no pipeline stage or new execution policy.''' + h[z:]\nh=h.replace('Retain the existing captured 34-bit D and 3D for the final radix-4 token, allowing synthesis to share duplicate register bits.', 'For the measured construction retain the existing captured 34-bit D and 3D fields in div_token_t; they are now unused by M and are pruned from the timed hardware. Keep their values available for current internal unit monitors. Do not resize or reorder the token bundle in this proposal.')\nh=h.replace('In each nonfinal round','In each round')\na=h.index('The original radix-4 logic is still required');z=h.index('\\\\n\\\\nPreserve magnitude',a)\nh=h[:a]+'''Remove both old radix-4 digits from alu.sv. During final_round, drive token.quotient=quotient_next and token.remainder=remainder_next; otherwise use the saved registers. If edge eight is blocked, save these COMPLETE values once and enter DIV_DONE. On a later consume, transfer the saved result without repeating the round. On immediate consume, transfer the same complete values and return to DIV_IDLE. In m_finish.sv, unsigned_div_result=remainder_op ? remainder : quotient; div_result=negate ? -unsigned_div_result : unsigned_div_result. This negation now starts from registered complete values and has no trial-subtraction/borrow-selection chain ahead of it. Preserve the existing M-kind mux and multiplication finalizer.''' + h[z:]\nh=h.replace('final-prefix availability', 'final-result availability')\nh=h.replace('Existing tests already check every registered four-bit prefix and must retain their exact latency, hold and reset assertions.', 'Existing tests check every registered four-bit prefix; retain those checks for edges one through seven. Update only the edge-eight token expectation from a thirty-bit prefix to full 32-bit unsigned quotient/remainder. Retain exact latency, hold, reset, source and result assertions. The old finalizer SAT test requires a boundary adapter: compute its reference final radix-4 digit from an arbitrary old prefix token, supply that COMPLETE token to the new m_finish, and prove the same architectural signed result. Keep the proof exhaustive over the original token inputs; do not delete or bypass it.')\na=h.index('The intended gain is shorter');h=h[:a]+'''A temporary implementation of this complete-result construction measured Gowin placement-option frequencies 81.549, 89.531 and 89.531 MHz, with a scored median of 89.531 MHz versus 81.140 MHz. Option-zero usage was 4,343 logic cells, 951 registers, 40 LUT RAMs, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. The worst median-option path moved to branch/recovery at 16.464 ns arrival; the radix-16 recurrence followed at 16.461 ns. Arrival includes clock contribution and is not the reciprocal of scored Fmax. At unchanged 4,239,051 CoreMark cycles, projected fitness is about 211.21, a 10.34 percent gain. The implementation evaluator must measure actual cycles and rerun every gate; this is not tournament acceptance.\n\nThe composed actual-arithmetic and ALTOPS ALU tests, arithmetic models and pipeline runner passed. The pre-existing finalizer-only SAT test initially failed because its input still described a thirty-bit prefix; after inserting the reference final-digit adapter for the new boundary, that exhaustive test passed. Strict Verilator lint passed after explicitly comparing elaboration-time modulo expressions against zero and naming conditional generate blocks. Those lint-only source corrections were made after the reported P&R run; rerun scored timing during implementation. Full formal and CoreMark checks are being attempted within the proposal budget; any completed results will be appended below. No assertion was weakened.\n\nAn earlier radix-16 prototype retained M's last radix-4 digit and measured only 81.879 MHz, below the acceptance margin. Implement the COMPLETE-result construction above, not that earlier prefix variant. The expected gain comes from removing the serial division work at both boundaries while keeping the same operation schedule. Added divisor-multiple registers and parallel subtractor routing are material risks, as are newly close branch, multiplier and ordinary-ALU forwarding paths. Acceptance requires measured fitness strictly above 200.21486, about 84.872 MHz at unchanged cycles. Temporary RTL and test edits are restored after research; this YAML is the deliverable.'''\nd['hypothesis']=h;d['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':10,'confidence':'medium'}\nd['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'Capture eight full-width odd divisor multiples; compute one radix-16 digit per round using fifteen parallel 37-bit native subtractions and a balanced candidate tree. Transfer complete unsigned quotient/remainder on edge eight or save them once if blocked. Remove both old radix-4 digits. Preserve divider protocol, nine-clock occupancy, real/ALTOPS timing and all other ALU operations.'},{'file':'rtl/m_finish.sv','description':'For real DIV/REM, select the registered complete quotient or remainder and apply the captured sign correction. Remove the final radix-4 trial subtraction and speculative signed-candidate tree. Preserve multiplication, ALTOPS, M-kind selection and the existing token port layout.'},{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Update div_token_t documentation to describe complete unsigned quotient/remainder rather than a thirty-bit prefix. Retain field order and widths, including now-unused divisor fields, to reproduce the measured construction and existing packed-layout monitors.'},{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Retain independent four-bit prefix checks for rounds one through seven, then check complete unsigned results in the edge-eight token. Adapt the exhaustive old-prefix finalizer proof by calculating the reference final digit before supplying a complete token to new m_finish. Add all sixteen radix-16 digits and threshold/width edge cases. Preserve exact latency, held-result, reset, early-consume, real/ALTOPS and composed architectural-result assertions.'}]\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=80));jsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')));print('Final construction written; schema valid.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
