{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_25", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml, json, jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r15s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-001-r15s0',\n'title':'Preselect the branch recovery address from captured prediction',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 202.72 at 85.936 MHz and 4,239,051 CoreMark cycles. After the radix-16 divider improvement, the reported worst path starts at ID/EX rs2 and ends at the fetch PC through EX recovery and front-end control. The actual branch comparison currently controls both redirect qualification and redirect_target selection. Earlier recovery simplifications were limited by arithmetic paths that the last three accepted changes have since shortened.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Factor the combinational EX recovery address away from the actual branch comparison. Keep resolved_pc_next unchanged for architectural RVFI reporting, but drive redirect_target from the registered prediction: predicted_taken selects pc+4, otherwise is_jalr selects the aligned rs1+imm target, otherwise use pc+imm. A redirect means actual_taken differs from predicted_taken, so this expression equals resolved_pc_next whenever IF can consume it. For predicted-taken recovery actual_taken is false; for predicted-not-taken recovery actual_taken is true. Preserve the existing redirect equation, prediction policy, comparator, alignment traps, predictor training, pipeline stages, forwarding and all bus handshakes. This is one local control/data mux optimization, not a new predictor or recovery stage.\n\nUse the existing native target additions and select between already computed targets; do not put branch_cond, actual_taken or redirect into the recovery-address data cone. The intended effect is to make comparison drive only the final PC redirect select rather than two serial target-selection levels. Keep PC repair on the same edge, exactly one killed younger slot, target faults and link suppression unchanged. Misaligned targets must still retire with the existing trap behavior and no forbidden redirect. Keep nret=1, all RV32IM and ALTOPS schedules, memory bounds, exact RVFI operands and contiguous order.\n\nCheck local equivalence: redirect implies new_redirect_target equals old resolved_pc_next for arbitrary operand, prediction, operation, validity and stall inputs. Exercise all six branch relations, both predictions, correct predictions, aligned/misaligned JAL/JALR, signed comparison boundaries and simultaneous instruction/data bus stalls. Run the unchanged pipeline, IF, formal/liveness and stalled CoreMark gates, preserving canonical CRCs, UART text and marker brackets. CoreMark cycle count should remain exactly 4,239,051; measure it. Acceptance requires fitness above 212.04512, or roughly 89.889 MHz if cycles are unchanged. Vendor timing must confirm the removed comparator-to-target-mux dependency rather than assume a win from RTL algebra. Competing divider recurrence and operand-bypass paths, shared-logic reconstruction and routing may limit the gain. This initial proposal has not yet been measured.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Separate architectural resolved_pc_next from the fetch recovery target. Preselect recovery_target using captured predicted_taken and jump type, with existing full-width native sums and JALR bit-zero clearing. Preserve redirect qualification, faults, training, arithmetic, latency and register update priorities.'},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Add directed recovery checks for both prediction directions, all branch comparisons, JAL/JALR alignment and stalled recovery. Require identical architectural PCs, links, traps, no wrong-path effects and unchanged retirement order and progress bounds.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=100))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Wrote and schema-validated',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
