{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_76", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,190p' tools/eval/formal.py\"", "aggregated_output": "\"\"\"Runs the real riscv-formal suite via formal/run_all.sh.\n\nThe real suite is generated at runtime by formal/run_all.sh (which invokes\ngenchecks.py against our rtl/*.sv + wrapper.sv + checks.cfg) and runs the\n~45 I-base / M-ext insn checks plus reg / pc_fwd / pc_bwd / causal /\nunique / cover / ill / liveness — 53 total against the V0 baseline.\n\nIf genchecks.py crashes mid-run and only emits one .sby task that\nvacuously passes, the old `passed > 0 and failed == 0` rule would\nreturn success. EXPECTED_MIN_CHECKS prevents that.\n\"\"\"\nimport os, shutil, subprocess, json, re, uuid\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport yaml\n\nfrom tools.eval._subprocess import run_pgroup\n\n\ndef read_nret(core_yaml_path: Path) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Read the `nret` field from a core.yaml. Defaults to 2 when the file\n    or field is missing — preserves backward compat with cores authored\n    before the nret-aware fixture (every existing core today).\n\n    Only 1 and 2 are supported. NRET=1 selects the single-issue formal\n    wrapper (wrapper_si.sv + checks_si.cfg); NRET=2 uses the dual-channel\n    default (wrapper.sv + checks.cfg).\n    \"\"\"\n    p = Path(core_yaml_path)\n    if not p.exists():\n        return 2\n    y = yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()) or {}\n    n = y.get(\"nret\", 2)\n    if n not in (1, 2):\n        raise ValueError(f\"core.yaml nret must be 1 or 2, got {n!r}\")\n    return n\n\n# Floor on how many .sby tasks must pass for a \"formal: green\" result.\n# V0 baseline produces 53. Allow some slack (≥50) so a future checks.cfg\n# tweak that legitimately drops 1-2 checks doesn't trigger a false alarm,\n# but reject a partial genchecks run that emits 1-2 tasks.\nEXPECTED_MIN_CHECKS = int(os.environ.get(\"FORMAL_MIN_CHECKS\", \"50\"))\n\n\n# Patterns that prove SBY actually executed at least one check before the\n# post-run `*.sby` glob came up empty. Any one of these in the output\n# means `no_checks_generated` is the wrong label — checks DID generate,\n# they just got wiped or interrupted between SBY's output and the tally.\n_SBY_RAN_PATTERNS = (\n    re.compile(r'^SBY \\d+:\\d+\n…[6147 of 9219 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b6a5670867345f21]…\n line.\n        tally = re.search(r'Formal:\\s+(\\d+)\\s+passed,\\s+(\\d+)\\s+failed', output)\n        if tally:\n            passed, failed = int(tally.group(1)), int(tally.group(2))\n            if failed > 0 or result.returncode != 0:\n                fail_line = re.search(r'Failed:\\s+(\\S+)', output)\n                failed_check = fail_line.group(1) if fail_line else 'unknown'\n                # `no_checks_generated` is run_all.sh's fallback when the\n                # post-run `for sby_file in *.sby` glob finds zero matches.\n                # That can mean genchecks.py crashed (the intended case) OR\n                # that something between genchecks and the tally, most\n                # commonly the implementer agent's bash tool, wiped or\n                # corrupted the checks directory mid-run. Distinguish so\n                # postmortems can tell \"tooling never produced checks\" from\n                # \"real SBY work happened then the directory was molested\".\n                if failed_check == 'no_checks_generated':\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_77", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r15s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-001-r15s0',\n'title':'Merge disjoint multiply limbs before a single carry-save reduction',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion reaches 202.72 fitness at 85.936 MHz and 4,239,051 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its radix-16 divider has exposed closely competing recovery, arithmetic bypass and multiply-completion paths. Fresh control-cone probes removed redundant branch dependencies but regressed median Fmax to 83.819 and 84.116 MHz while multiply completion became critical. The current m_finish describes four overlapping 64-bit operands and two carry-save reductions, although the low-low product has only 32 meaningful bits and two terms can be merged into disjoint lanes.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Optimize only the real-arithmetic multiplication finalizer in m_finish.sv. Keep the four existing signed 17-by-17 limb products, their EX/MEM registers, operation tags and all instruction latencies. Replace the two 64-bit carry-save reductions with one 48-bit reduction by first merging non-overlapping LL and HH fields. This is one local arithmetic representation optimization; it changes no pipeline, bypass policy, predictor or divider.\n\nThe multiplier operands a_lo and b_lo are signed 17-bit values with bit 16 fixed at zero. Hence LL=a_lo*b_lo is nonnegative, fits 32 bits, and mul_partial.ll[33:32] are always zero for real captured products. The low 16 product bits are exactly LL[15:0], since every other partial product starts at bit 16 or above. The product above bit 15 is therefore LH + HL + (HH << 16) + LL[31:16], modulo 2\"'^48. The last two terms occupy disjoint lanes and can be concatenated rather than added.\n\nUse exactly three 48-bit terms:\n  term_lh = {{14{mul_partial.lh[33]}}, mul_partial.lh};\n  term_hl = {{14{mul_partial.hl[33]}}, mul_partial.hl};\n  term_ll_hh = {mul_partial.hh[31:0], mul_partial.ll[31:16]}.\nCompute sum = term_lh ''^ term_hl ''^ term_ll_hh and\ncarry = ((term_lh & term_hl) | (term_lh & term_ll_hh) |\n         (term_hl & term_ll_hh)) << 1, both at exactly 48 bits.\nSet upper_product = sum + carry using one native 48-bit addition;\nproduct = {upper_product, mul_partial.ll[15:0]}.\nKeep the existing high_word selection of product[63:32] versus\nproduct[31:0], and the existing M-kind output mux. Dropping HH bits\nabove 31 is exact because their original shift by 32 places them\noutside the retained 64-bit product. Preserve signed LH/HL extension\nBEFORE addition; treating those cross terms as unsigned corrupts MULH\nand MULHSU. Do not reintroduce a separate LL-upper addition, which\nwould restore the removed arithmetic level.\n\nLeave alu.sv, core_pkg.sv, all packed field widths/order, partial-product capture enables and reset behavior unchanged. Keep the entire RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS branch unchanged: it bypasses real multiplication and cannot establish this arithmetic identity. Leave real/ALTOPS division, M completion scheduling, X pending hazards, forwarding, memory side effects, traps, nret=1 and all RVFI fields unchanged. The new finalizer consumes only the registered EX/MEM token, including while younger M operations run or memory stalls hold that token.\n\nA temporary implementation of precisely this construction measured Gowin option frequencies 92.189, 91.009 and 91.009 MHz, median 91.009 MHz versus the champion'\"'s 85.936 MHz. The option-zero mapping uses 4,452 logic cells, 951 registers, 40 LUT RAMs, four BSRAMs and three DSPs; the champion uses 4,380 logic cells, the same register/memory counts and two DSPs. Thus this is a timing-for-area trade, not a DSP reduction claim. The median-option worst path is now the divider recurrence at 16.282 ns arrival; option zero is limited by branch/bypass control at 16.142 ns. Vendor arrival includes clock contribution and is not the reciprocal of scored Fmax. At unchanged CoreMark cycles, projected fitness is approximately 214.69, about 5.9 percent above the champion.\n\nA Yosys SAT miter proved the optimized real finalizer equal to the independent 64-bit expression LL + (signed(LH)<<16) + (signed(HL)<<16) + (signed(HH)<<32) for every 32-bit LL, arbitrary signed 34-bit LH/HL/HH and both high_word values. The only input restriction is LL[33:32]=0, a guarantee of the existing zero-extended 16-bit low limbs. There are no sign or reachability restrictions on the cross/high terms. Preserve this proof as an additional test rather than replacing existing division equivalence tests. Validate the low-low width guarantee separately from the actual alu limb declarations or a local proof. Strict Verilator lint passed. Additional arithmetic, pipeline and stalled CoreMark validation is in progress; append completed results before implementation.\n\nExtend real MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU tests with all-zero/all-one limbs, 0x0000ffff/0x00010000 boundaries, signed extrema, opposite signs, low-middle carry propagation, high-half carries and back-to-back M operations under holds. Retain every existing exact-result, latency, reset, hold and ALTOPS assertion. Run unchanged formal/liveness and stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker gates. Expected cycles are exactly 4,239,051; measure them. Acceptance requires measured fitness strictly above 212.04512, about 89.889 MHz at unchanged cycles. The proposal-stage timing clears this threshold but is not tournament acceptance. The margin is modest, extra DSP inference is a material mapping change, and divider/control paths remain close competitors. Do not add unrelated control-cone changes. Temporary RTL probes will be restored; the sole deliverable is this YAML.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[{'file':'rtl/m_finish.sv','description':'Merge HH[31:0] and LL[31:16] into a 48-bit disjoint-lane term; sign-extend LH and HL to 48 bits; perform one three-input carry-save reduction and one native addition; concatenate LL[15:0] to reconstruct the product. Preserve high/low selection, M-kind mux, divider, ALTOPS and all interfaces/latency.'},{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Add real multiply limb/carry/sign boundary vectors and a local SAT equivalence test for the actual optimized finalizer against the independent four-term 64-bit product expression, constraining only LL[33:32] to the zeros guaranteed by the existing low-limb multipliers. Retain all existing multiply/divide, composed-pipeline, timing, hold, reset, ALTOPS and equivalence checks.'}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=100))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Wrote and schema-validated final-angle hypothesis:',p)\nprint('Projected fitness:',91.009e6*10/4239051)\nprint('Delta percent:',(91.009/85.936-1)*100)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
