d\\nquotient or remainder before transferring the instruction to EX/MEM.\\nEach restoring step uses one extended subtract and its borrow to select\\nthe next remainder. Separate magnitude preparation and sign correction\\nfrom the four arithmetic rounds: accept and latch magnitudes at edge 0,\\nrun rounds at edges 1 through 4, register the corrected res\n…[187064 of 190136 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:07bb5de536267573]…\n.2, \"delta_pct\": 4.59, \"vs_baseline\": 1551.82, \"fmax_mhz\": 79.967, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3994432, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4153, \"ff\": 945, \"seeds\": [78.526, 79.967, 79.967], \"perturbations\": [[0, 78.526, 17], [1, 79.967, 18], [2, 79.967, 18]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_31_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_6_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -7.735, \"arrival_ns\": 18.029, \"logic_cells\": 65, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 17, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T23:29:22.643881Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-002-r14s1 (regression, +4.59%): A separate-pointer, masked-OR instruction ring timed better than compaction or nested head muxes, but its read-pointer-to-register-file-to-ID/EX path still competes with bypass and divider paths, leaving the stall-overlap throughput gain below the 4.6% acceptance margin.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
