ucture only EX's predictor-recovery\n  fanout so the late branch outcome determines whether to redirect, while the saved\n  prediction independently selects the correction address and conditional branch faults\n  cannot affect fetch holds through forwarding eligibility.\n\n  In rtl/ex_stage.sv retain the current actual_taken, resolved_pc_next, ex_advance and\n  direction-mismatch redirect predicate. Replace only the correction-address assignment\n  with:\n    redirect_target = in.predicted_taken ? (in.pc + 32'd4)\n                    : (in.ctrl.is_jump ? jump_target : branch_target);\n  All operands of this address selection come from the already registered instruction, PC,\n  immediate, resolved rs1 and prediction. Keep the full-width PC+4, branch target and jump\n  target computations available in parallel; do not preselect an offset before a share\n…[4522 of 7594 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2fbd6624a6189bfb]…\nmedium\nchanges:\n- file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n  description: |-\n    Select the correction target from the saved predicted_taken bit, using parallel PC+4 and\n    resolved branch/jump targets, while retaining authoritative resolved_pc_next for RVFI.\n    Define EX writer eligibility from registered valid/legal/reg_write controls and\n    misalign_jump only, removing conditional branch outcome from forwarding-induced fetch\n    holds. Keep the existing redirect predicate, architectural trap payload and predictor\n    training unchanged.\n- file: test/test_pipeline.py\n  description: |-\n    Preserve existing predictor and architectural assertions. Add focused recovery cases for\n    both direction errors, branch versus JALR alignment faults, dependent link use, imem-\n    stalled/dmem-release recovery, and wrong-path stores/divides. Check the correction\n    address only when redirect is asserted and retain exact resolved RVFI PC/trap/link\n    values, once-only training, one-slot miss behavior and the unchanged progress bound.\n", "exit_c